INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5065265', 'Charley Palmer Rothwell was born on February 9, 1992 in Bethnal Green, London, England. He is an actor, known for Dunkirk (2017), Legend (2015) and iBoy (2017).::Anonymous', 'Charley Palmer', 'Rothwell', '1992-02-09', NULL, 'Charley Palmer Rothwell');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6067087', 'Tom Gill was born on June 30, 1989 in Salford, Manchester, England. He is an actor, known for Eden Lake (2008), Dunkirk (2017) and Squadron 42 (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1989-06-30', NULL, 'Tom Gill');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('7351526', 'Sam Aronow is an American-Israeli actor and director. He was born Sam Aronow Huddy on December 18, 1989, in Pasadena, California, to Denise Aronow and Robert Huddy, and has both Jewish and Irish ancestry. Aronow credits his mother as his main influence to become a filmmaker, claiming that she guided him toward the career by making him watch Close Encounters of the Third Kind (1977) at the age of ten. He began writing and directing short videos with his friends, as well as writing feature-length scripts, but lost them after successive computer crashes.Huddy attended film school at San Francisco State University and later California State University, Los Angeles with the intent of writing for television, but began acting in order to assist his classmates (notably Gene Aversa). After graduating in 2014, Huddy took his maternal grandfather''s name Sam Aronow, completed his first short film Character (2016), and began acting professionally, mostly as an extra, before emigrating to Israel to work in the film industry there.::samhuddy', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sam Aronow');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6983738', 'Simon Ates is an actor, known for Dunkirk (2017), Fataal (2016) and Dark Machine (2016).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Simon Ates');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6498873', 'Caleb Bailey is known for his work on Battle of the Sexes (2017) and Dunkirk (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Caleb Bailey');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8394965', 'Aldo Beqiri was born on July 14, 1992 in Lushnjë, Albania. He is known for his work on King Arthur: Legend of the Sword (2017) and Dunkirk (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1992-07-14', NULL, 'Aldo Beqiri');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6753446', 'Paul was born in Lake Havasu City, AZ in 1984. He then became a state ranked diver in Indiana, and trained alongside Olympians. He decided to begin pursuing an acting career immediately after high school and moved to sunny Las Vegas. After an 8 year stint of odd jobs, including the notable off-Broadway show, Tony n Tina''s Wedding, he finally made the move to L.A. Now he''s working in television and film, and has sights set high.::Paul Fox', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Paul Riley Fox');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6147904', 'Jack Gover was born on February 5, 1991 in Southampton Hampshire. He is of English decent. Jack was bought up in Nursling Southampton and attended Mountbatten school in Romsey. Jack spent his childhood and teenage years competing in motorsport , mentored by his father (Michael Gover) . In 2012 Jack was cast as a young police officer in ''Fred Dinenage murder casebook''. The following year was cast as Conrad in his first feature length ''Out For Revenge'' (2013) . This lead on to a leading roles in feature films, TV and short films.::Jack Gover', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jack Gover');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8427461', 'Sander Huisman is an actor, known for Dunkirk (2017), The Perfect Shot (2014) and Sinterklaasjournaal (2001).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sander Huisman');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8547144', 'Samgar Jacobs is known for his work on King Arthur: Legend of the Sword (2017) and Dunkirk (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Samgar Jacobs');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8280585', 'Christian Janner was born on January 2, 1993 in Denmark. He is an actor and editor, known for Dunkirk (2017), Little Star (2016) and Pure Genius (2016).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1993-01-02', NULL, 'Christian Janner');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5367048', 'Jedediah Jenk, all-around storyteller, began his journey with an early fascination in theater and film. As a mere child, he was chosen to play "Tiny Tim" in a local Christmas production and received a standing ovation. Jedediah was not merely satisfied with playing a character on the stage. By only the 6th grade, he was composing feature-film orchestral compositions and writing full-length screenplays. Peers and teachers looked on in amazement, voting him "mostly likely to succeed." The name "Jedi" began to stick as he as he explored his many film-related talents. Jedi was also revered for his tech-savvy, often volunteering to help with computer repairs.By the time he was of college-age, Jedi was already working at the highly prestigious Skywalker Sound in northern California and was hand-picked for a unique film internship in Germany. Inspired by his family''s history of engineers, Jedi explored sound design and orchestral scoring for film. However, drawn to a deep love of the ultimate story-telling art, Jedi decided to take back to his root in acting and briefly moved to NY to study with famed casting director John Pallotta. Jedi moved back to LA in 2015 to continue his acting education with fellow actors Reynaldo Pacheco and Joy Rinaldi and casting director Sam Christinsen.To date, Jedediah Jenk has acted with some of the best in the business - including Tom Hanks and Emma Watson and worked with top directors Christopher Nolan, Dean Deblois and Clint Eastwood. Jedesiah studied under iconic and well-loved film composers Alan Silvestri and Shigeru Umebayashi."Always push forward to be the best you that you can be! Life goes by very quickly and we owe it to ourselves to make the most of it and to love and inspire others to do the same!" - Jedediah, 2017Jedediah''s passion for storytelling is matched only by his love for people and his desire to use film and acting as a tool of inspiration. Jedediah has been involved with several charities such as Breast Cancer Foundations and frequently donates his time to various charitable organizations.After working briefly in the background world to explore a new side of film, meet otherwise forgotten people and earn his way, from the bottom-up into SAG-AFTRA, Jedediah "The Jedi" is poised to become one of the most successful rising stars of our generation - combining intellect, compassion, passion, and creativity into one package.::Jedediah Jenk''s PR Team', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jedediah Jenk');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('9046360', 'Han Leopold is known for his work on Ron Goossens, Low Budget Stuntman (2017), Dunkirk (2017) and De Familie Slim (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Han Leopold');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4074525', 'Valiant was raised by prominent Farmers and Land Owners in a Midwest farming community originally owned and named after Pioneer and State Legislator Sebastian Kronenwetter. He showed a strong interest in the arts especially in music and theatre at a very early age.His most daring venture to date was being a Steampunk Aviator Male Model on the runway for Fashion Designer and Producer (Fashion Forward) Leonard Simpson''s "10 Best Dressed Awards and Fashion Show" and Dress for Success Charity 2014 at Hilton La Jolla Torrey Pines in La Jolla, CA. Since 2015, Valiant has been a male model for Michael Kors Mens Designer Suits and Tuxedos in The Los Angeles Fashion Shows on a monthly basis.For three decades, Valiant has been involved in numerous acting venues from Theatre to Reenactments to TV Series to Movies. He has acted in Civil War Reenactments(North Union Regiment Captain),Revolutionary War Reenactments(American Militia Fighter),Renaissance Festival Performances(Swordsman),Shakespeare in the Park(Prince Escalus of Verona), Pirate Faire performances (Pirate),The Go Game Corporate Role play games (Mobster or Pirate), and various Steampunk characters.Valiant earned his B.A degree in English Education (Magna Cum Laude) at MSC in 1996. He taught University Level English Literature under the direction of MSC Dean and Professor of English Dr. Vincent Beach, Ph.D. and Graduate Professorship Recommendations from Education Chair Dr. John Eitenmiller, Ph.D., Professor of English Dr. Bruce Glassco, Ph.D., MSC College President Dr. John Cable, Ph.D., and MSC Dean of Academics and Professor of English Dr. Victor Macaruso, Ph.D. Valiant was in theatre during those college years as various characters and performed with other actors in "Shakespeare in the Park" as Prince Escalus of Verona.Valiant went on to Graduate School for a M.A in English Education at Bemidji State University but left after a year due to a "boring and repetitious curriculum". He continued his graduate work and earned two Doctorates through UET via University of Minnesota in 2002. Valiant decided to pursue careers as a Book Editor, Novel Writer, Actor, and Musician instead of a University Professor.::CC', 'Michael Christian', 'Valiant', '1974-07-02', NULL, 'Valiant Michael');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8201661', 'Thomas Millet is known for his work on King Arthur: Legend of the Sword (2017) and Dunkirk (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Thomas Millet');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1720532', 'Johnny Otto is the ultimate multi-hyphenate: He is an American Film Director, Writer, Actor, Game Designer, iOS Developer, Photographer, Animation Director, Artist and Musician living in Los Angeles, CA. He attended University in Windsor, Ontario Canada from 1988 - 1990, taught the Film Production Lab there for two semesters and then moved to Los Angeles in 1990 to pursue his creative interests. Johnny is known for his quirky and unique films, and for shooting in a loose, improvisational way similar to such noted Directors as Woody Allen and the French cinéma vérité movement.In 1992 Otto option his first feature-length script entitled Havoc to Producer Joel Silver. A few years later, in 1998, Otto wrote a dark comedy called Pop Life, which got the attention of agents over at Innovative Artists and the film was being packaged with hot, young talent. But, in 1999 Otto hit a stumbling block when production of "Pop Life", closely resembling the Columbine Shootings, was halted. Actress Rachael Leigh Cook who was set to star as a troubled cheerleader, withdrew from the project and, because of the sensitive nature of the subject material, the film was never made.Otto persevered and In 2001 completed his first animation project The Blender and won an award from The 8th World Animation Celebration (WACFEST - Animation Magazine). In 2006 he began production on his feature-length mockumentary, Bring Me The Head of Walt Disney, which he finished a year later in 2007. In the fall of 2007 Otto shot 7 short films in a 7 week period, one film every Sunday afternoon, and calls the project Slimdunce. In 2015 Otto began work on his first 4k film, The Sun King, which will be completed by September.::Johnny Otto', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Johnny Otto');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8248536', 'Crystal Pereyra was born on December 10 1998, in Boston, Massachussetts. She is an upcoming actress best known for her role in Dunkirk (2017). At a young age, she attended seasonal acting classes at Barbizon USA after having sparked a sudden interest in acting. Raised by two loving parents and accompanied by her two sisters, Crystal spent most of her early years in Boston.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Crystal Pereyra');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8495697', 'Robby Prinsen is known for his work on King Arthur: Legend of the Sword (2017), Dunkirk (2017) and Redbad (2018).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Robby Prinsen');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5759069', 'Sandhya Chandel is an actress, known for Spirit in the Woods (2014), Captain America: The Winter Soldier (2014) and Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sandhya Chandel');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4149902', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Russell Levine');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('7051642', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Heather Cooley');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1807993', 'It all began when Christian was approached by an acting teacher at a movie theater in Phoenix, Arizona.Christian started out doing Improvisation on stage in the group known as ''Impromptu''. Subsequently, Christian eventually obtained a college degree in Liberal Arts and Sciences. The Actor/Model/Singer/Whistler has experience working in Film, TV, Print, Theatre/Stage, Video Game Industry (*motion capture), & Voice Over.::anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1985-02-24', NULL, 'Christian Roberts');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('7323402', 'Jan-Michael Rosner is an actor, known for The Heist (2017), Parks and Recreation (2009) and Dunkirk (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jan-Michael Rosner');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6762004', 'Connor Ryan was born April 18, 1990 in Doylestown, Pennsylvania. He is the son of Danielle Lee McStravock an accomplished saleswoman, and George Geib, a Helicopter Pilot, and is mostly of German, Choctaw Indian, Irish, and English ancestry. He started playing guitar at age 12, and later formed the music duo Circuit to the Moon along with Richard J. Amtmann III. He enrolled at Bucks County Community College to study Film/Video production. After meeting Davron Mananov in College he started acting in O.Y.M.P, a web series created by Mananov where they filmed a movie a day for a full year. Since then he has appeared in films, television, music videos, commercials, and web series.::Connor Ryan', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Connor Ryan');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6391889', 'Michiel van Ieperen was born in Nieuwegein, Utrecht on June 23, 1989, to a Dutch-born mother, Marry van Beuzekom, and a Dutch-born father, Kiek van Ieperen, an Olympic Skeet-shooter who was on the official Dutch Skeet-shooting team from 1973 till 1993, and still Dutch record-holder with six World Cup and Europe Cup-medals.As a kid, van Ieperen always had strong feelings towards film. Playing with old camera''s, recording stuff with friends ''just for fun'', watching countless of films over and over again, and ''constantly rewinding scenes on his VHS to get a sense how they did it''. Never even thinking about the possibility of becoming an actor or director in the Netherlands, and not wanting to take over the family business (his grandfather and father had their own construction company), van Ieperen had the dream of becoming a journalist. He began his academic career in 2008 at the University of Amsterdam, where he studied Communication Studies. However, during his time in Amsterdam, van Ieperen''s passion for film resurfaced. During his bachelor''s degree, van Ieperen began working as an editor, producer and PR- and marketing consultant for the Dutch premium cable film- and television network Film1/Sport1, a division of the Chellomedia network.Graduating his BA in 2011, van Ieperen was determined to continue following his ambition to work in the film-industry, and applied for a MA-course at the Dutch Film-academy in Amsterdam. However, van Ieperen was denied on the basis of ''not having enough experience''. Down, but not out, van Ieperen searched for a alternative route to achieve his goals, which he found at the University of Utrecht, where he began following a MA in Film- and Television Studies. While studying for his Master''s, van Ieperen started working as a producer for Eyeworks Group, one of the biggest film- and television production companies in Europe.During his Master''s in Utrecht and his behind-the-scenes work at Eyeworks, van Ieperen became more interested in acting, and the process of an actor. Graduating his MA in the summer of 2013, he still had a creative itch to scratch, and started attending several acting workshops in Amsterdam. This however, wasn''t enough for van Ieperen. Always wanting to go the United States, but never having a chance to do so, now was the time. He packed his bags, and moved to Los Angeles, where he followed an actor''s course at the New York Film Academy. Here, van Ieperen truly fell in love with acting and filmmaking. This all led to his first lead acting-project, a 16-minute short film called "Sides", was selected to be shown at the 2014 edition of the famous film festival Cannes in the category Short Film Corner.Since returning to the Netherlands in the spring of 2014, van Ieperen has been working non-stop as in actor in dozens of different projects, ranging from commercials, to shorts and music videos. His first feature film roles where for the Dutch drama "Fataal" & "Dunkirk" by Christopher Nolan.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Michiel van Ieperen');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8649765', 'Bram Vlot is known for his work on King Arthur: Legend of the Sword (2017), Dunkirk (2017) and Centraal Medisch Centrum (2016).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Bram Vlot');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8310330', 'Olav Vollebregt is an actor, known for Dunkirk (2017) and Sense8 (2015).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Olav Vollebregt');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6592699', 'Nick Vorsselman was born on February 27, 1996 in Epe, Gelderland, Netherlands. He is known for his work on Dunkirk (2017), Goede tijden, slechte tijden (1990) and The Hitman''s Bodyguard (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1996-02-27', NULL, 'Nick Vorsselman');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6062133', 'Merlijn was born on December 18th 1999 in Haarlem, the Netherlands. In 2007 he moved to Zutphen, the Netherlands where he got his first video camera and started to make short movies with it. In 2012 he started making short movies with friends, his first production was a clip about the city he lives in, Zutphen. In the years that followed, he started making short fiction movies. He always planned to become an actor, until he realized that he only wanted that to be able to do something with film. He realized he wanted to become a director, until last year. He realized that he always focuses on getting the perfect image. Merlijn wants to become a cinematographer now and is planning to go to the Dutch Filmacademy and study cinematography.::Merlijn Willemsen', NULL, NULL, '1999-12-18', NULL, 'Merlijn Willemsen');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('7359346', 'Nirman Wolf is known for his work on Zomers Blijven Niet (2016), Fataal (2016) and Peer (2015).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Nirman Wolf');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2857718', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Trevor Christie');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1418292', 'Wesley Coller is a producer, known for 300 (2006), Man of Steel (2013) and Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wesley Coller');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0424315', 'Geoff Johns is an American comic book and television writer, film and television producer.He is the Chief Creative Officer at DC Comics, a position he has served in since 2010. His most notable work in different media has used the DC Comics characters Green Lantern, Aquaman, The Flash and Superman.In 2006, Johns co-wrote the story for the Justice League Unlimited episode "Ancient History", which starred Hawkman, Hawkgirl, Vixen, Shadow Thief and the Green Lantern John Stewart.Johns served as a co-producer and creative consultant for Green Lantern (2011) directed by Martin Campbell and starring Ryan Reynolds.He is an executive producer on Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016), directed by Zack Snyder and starring Henry Cavill and Ben Affleck.As of mid-2015, Johns and Ben Affleck are co-writing the screenplay for a standalone Batman film.::Pedro Borges', NULL, NULL, '1973-01-25', NULL, 'Geoff Johns');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2294683', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Curt Kanemoto');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0605337', 'Bruce Moriarty was born as Bruce Gerald Moriarty. He is an assistant director and producer, known for Forrest Gump (1994), Casino Royale (2006) and Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016).::Anonymous', 'Bruce Gerald', 'Moriarty', NULL, NULL, 'Bruce Moriarty');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0746541', 'Jim Rowe is a Producer and Unit Production Manager, known for "Godzilla" (2014)/Director Gareth Edwards, "Man of Steel" (2013)/Director Zack Snyder, "Sucker Punch"(2011)/Director Zack Snyder, "Red Riding Hood" (2011)/Director Catherine Hardwicke, "Watchmen" (2009)/Director Zack Snyder, "Hot Rod" (2007)/Director Akiva Schaffer, "Underworld: Evolution" (2006)/Director Len Wiseman and "Are We There Yet" (2005)/Director Brian Levant to name a few. He has been working in the film industry since 1988.::AS', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jim Rowe');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2003463', 'Deborah Snyder was born as Deborah Johnson. She is a producer, known for 300 (2006), Man of Steel (2013) and Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016). She has been married to Zack Snyder since September 25, 2004.::Anonymous', 'Deborah', 'Johnson', NULL, NULL, 'Deborah Snyder');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0921600', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Andrea Wertheim');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0933470', 'Gregor Wilson is known for his work on Inglourious Basterds (2009), Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016) and Man of Steel (2013).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Gregor Wilson');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0010736', 'Amy Lou Adams was born in Vicenza, Veneto, Italy, to American parents, Kathryn (Hicken) and Richard Kent Adams, a U.S. serviceman who was stationed at Caserma Ederle in Italy at the time. She was raised in a Mormon family of seven children in Castle Rock, Colorado, and has English, as well as smaller amounts of Danish, Swiss-German, and Norwegian, ancestry.Adams sang in the school choir at Douglas County High School and was an apprentice dancer at a local dance company, with the ambition of becoming a ballerina. However, she worked as a greeter at The Gap and as a Hooters hostess to support herself before finding work as a dancer at Boulder''s Dinner Theatre and Country Dinner Playhouse in such productions as "Brigadoon" and "A Chorus Line". It was there that she was spotted by a Minneapolis dinner-theater director who asked her to move to Chanhassen, Minnesota for more regional dinner theater work.Nursing a pulled muscle that kept her from dancing, she was free to audition for a part in Bella da morire (1999), which was filming nearby in Minnesota. During the filming, Kirstie Alley encouraged her to move to Los Angeles, where she soon won a part in the Fox television version of the film, Cruel Intentions (1999), in the part played in the film by Sarah Michelle Gellar, "Kathryn Merteuil". Although three episodes were filmed, the troubled series never aired. Instead, parts of the episodes were cobbled together and released as the direct-to-video Cruel Intentions 2 (2000). After more failed television spots, she landed a major role in Catch Me If You Can (2002), playing opposite Leonardo DiCaprio. But this did not provide the break-through she might have hoped for, with no work being offered for about a year. She eventually returned to television, and joined the short-lived series, Dr. Vegas (2004).Her role in the low-budget independent film Junebug (2005) (which was shot in 21 days) got her real attention, including an Academy Award nomination for Best Supporting Actress as well as other awards. The following year, her ability to look like a wide-eyed Disney animated heroine helped her to be chosen from about 300 actresses auditioning for the role of "Giselle" in the animated/live-action feature film, Enchanted (2007), which would prove to be her major break-through role. Her vivacious yet innocent portrayal allowed her to use her singing and dancing talents. Her performance garnered a Golden Globe Award nomination for Best Actress in a Motion Picture Musical or Comedy.Adams next appeared in the major production, Charlie Wilson''s War (2007), and went on to act in the independent film, Sunshine Cleaning (2008), which premiered at the 2008 Sundance Film Festival. Her role as "Sister James" in Doubt (2008) brought her a second Academy Award nomination for Best Supporting Actress, as well as nominations for a Golden Globe, a Screen Actors Guild award, and a British Academy Film award. She appeared as Amelia Earhart in Night at the Museum: Battle of the Smithsonian (2009) and as a post-9/11 hot line counselor, aspiring writer, amateur cook and blogger in Julie & Julia (2009). In the early 2010s, she starred with Jason Segel in The Muppets (2011), with Philip Seymour Hoffman in Paul Thomas Anderson''s The Master (2012), and alongside Clint Eastwood and Justin Timberlake in Trouble with the Curve (2012). She played reporter Lois Lane in Man of Steel (2013) and con artist Sydney Prosser in American Hustle (2013), before portraying real-life artist Margaret Keane in Tim Burton''s biopic Big Eyes (2014).In 2016, she reprised her role as Lane in Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016), and headlined Denis Villeneuve''s science fiction drama Arrival (2016) and Tom Ford''s dark thriller Nocturnal Animals (2016).::Brian Greenhalgh', 'Amy Lou', 'Adams', '1974-08-20', NULL, 'Amy Adams');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0251986', 'Curly haired and with a fast-talking voice, Jesse Eisenberg is a movie actor, known for his Academy Award nominated role as Mark Zuckerberg in the 2010 film The Social Network. He has also starred in the films The Squid and the Whale, Adventureland, The Education of Charlie Banks, 30 Minutes or Less, Now You See Me and Zombieland. Additionally, he played Lex Luthor in the 2016 film Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice.Jesse Adam Eisenberg was born on October 5, 1983 in Queens, New York, and was raised in East Brunswick Township, New Jersey. His mother, Amy (Fishman), is a professional dressed-up clown who performed at children''s birthday parties for a living in their hometown of East Brunswick for 20 years. His father, Barry Eisenberg, ran a hospital before moving on to become a college professor. Jesse has two sisters, Kerri and Hallie Kate Eisenberg, who was a popular child star. His family is Jewish (his ancestors came to the U.S. from Poland, Russia, and Ukraine).He attended East Brunswick High School, but he didn''t really enjoy school. From age 10, he performed in children''s theater. Jesse had his first professional role in an off-Broadway play, "The Gathering". Before fame, he made his first television appearance role that came in 1999 when he was 16 with a show on Fox''s Get Real (1999), but the show was canceled in 2000. In his senior year of high school, he had landed his first film leading role in the 2002 film Roger Dodger (2002). He won an award for "Most Promising New Actor" at the San Diego film festival.Jesse attended the New School University, New York, where he was a liberal arts major, with a focus on Democracy and Cultural Pluralism. He also studied at The New School in New York City''s Greenwich Village. He applied and was accepted to New York University but declined enrollment to complete a film role. He has been playing the drums since he was age 8.His breakthrough role came in Zombieland (2009). In 2010, he was nominated for Best Actor at the Golden Globes and Academy Awards for his role of Facebook''s creator, Mark Zuckerberg, in the film, The Social Network (2010). He also voiced Blu, a rare blue macaw, in the film Rio (2011), and its sequel Rio 2 (2014). He starred alongside Aziz Ansari in the 2011 comedy 30 Minutes Or Less, and played himself in the 2013 comedy film He''s Way More Famous Than You (2013).::crazymoviereviewer', 'Jesse Adam', 'Eisenberg', '1983-10-05', NULL, 'Jesse Eisenberg');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1547787', 'Tiffany L. Addison is an actress and producer, known for Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016), The Break-Up (2006) and Barbershop 2: Back in Business (2004).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Tiffany L. Addison');
