INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1600560', 'Gus Lewis was born on January 19, 1993 in New York City, New York, USA. He is an actor, known for Batman Begins (2005), Asylum (2005) and One for Sorrow (2009).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1993-01-19', NULL, 'Gus Lewis');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3565825', 'An Army Veteran and New Jersey native, Joe Lipari has been performing stand up since 2003 when he first took the stage at the world famous Caroline''s on Broadway.Since then Joe has spent 2 years on Sirius Satellite Radio with Dee Snider (Twisted Sister), produced countless TV commercials, worked on MTV''s hit reality shows The Hills & The City, had his photography published, and made a name for himself in New York City''s competitive comedy scene.::The Improv Hollywood', NULL, NULL, '1979-10-05', NULL, 'Joe Lipari');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4774305', 'Jeremy Long is a writer, actor and comic, perhaps best known for his 2014 documentary film Tenacity and Gratitude: The Frank Cotolo Story (2014). Jeremy was born in Pennsylvania and graduated from Palmyra Area High School in 2010, at which point he furthered his education at Penn State University, majoring in film with a minor in theater. After graduating from Pennsylvania State University, Jeremy moved to Los Angeles, California to further his career in film. Throughout his career, Jeremy has acted in theater, stage plays and film & television He has also toured the country as a stand-up comic, performing everywhere from NYC to Los Angeles. In addition to stand-up comedy, Jeremy is also a member of the highly sought after improv troupe High Fructose Imporov, formed in 2011. In 2010, Jeremy co-founded the independent production company Winston Simmons Productions, which is still active to this day. Then, in November 2011, Jeremy received his very first feature film role in Jack Reacher (2012) starring Tom Cruise. Afterwards, Jeremy continued to act in both film and television, perhaps most notably in Me and Earl and the Dying Girl (2015). In 2014, Jeremy released his very first feature film under his production company, Winston Simmons Productions, titled Tenacity and Gratitude: The Frank Cotolo Story (2014) which is a documentary directed, produced, written and edited by Jeremy Long about his friend and mentor Frank Cotolo who is a renowned entertainer and has written for all the great comics of the last few decades, as well as being Wolfman Jack''s longtime writer and radio partner. Jeremy currently resides in Los Angeles, California where he is working for Field''s Entertainment, founded by legendary producer Simon Fields, in Post Production for the television series The Carbonaro Effect (2014) on TruTv. Jeremy also continues to act, being featured in episodes of classic television shows such as Do No Harm (2013), NCIS (2003), Mom (2013), and The Goldbergs (2013), as well as new hit shows such as The Muppets (2015), Code Black (2015), and Supergirl (2015), among others. Jeremy also continues to perform comedy and improv to audiences everywhere. Jeremy is currently in pre-production of a television series titled The Return of Turk Berain (2016), which he co-wrote with writing partner Frank Cotolo and is based on Cotolo''s book of the same name. Jeremy is also in pre-production for his second feature film The Unfortunate Monsters (2017), an apocalyptic drama film which he wrote and will produce.::Anonymous', 'Jeremy Michael Dunkin', 'Long', '1992-03-12', NULL, 'Jeremy Long');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5336195', 'Amos Mac is a producer and actor, known for The Trans List (2016), Kate Bornstein is a Queer & Pleasant Danger (2014) and The Carrie Diaries (2013).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Amos Mac');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5332621', 'Oscar was born and raised in Biggs-Gridley, CA. The eldest of 4 siblings; Oscar is the son of migrant farm workers from Mexico. He grew up farming Kiwifruit and Sugar Plums; and later studied Ag-Engineering at CSU, Chico. While living in Chico, Oscar played in amateur football leagues while going to school. Deciding that football was not his true passion; Oscar rediscovered his childhood love of theater. From 2007-2010, he participated in several musicals and has performed live over 100 times. Using this foundation, Oscar decided to move to L.A. to pursue acting as a career. He joined SAG-AFTRA in 2011 and has worked in the industry for 4 years in various roles and capacities. Also during this time, Oscar studied the art of film making and visual effects. Seeking to diversify, he is committed to knowing the craft from all angles and hopes to bring Hollywood to his hometown area. Over the years, Oscar has had the privilege of working on set with most A-list actors and Directors and is grateful for being a part of such an exciting industry.::Author', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Oscar Magana Jr.');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3704938', 'Jack Mahrt was born in Dayton, Ohio. Later the family moved north of Dayton to the city of Piqua. Jack attended and graduated Lehman High School in Sidney, Ohio. He has a degree in radio/tv broadcasting-communication arts. Mahrt is a veteran of the U.S. Navy and was deployed in combat overseas. After his service in the Navy, Jack returned back to Ohio to work in law enforcement. For a period of time, he was employed as a corrections officer at the Miami County Sheriff''s Office in Troy, Ohio. Later, Jack attended the Federal Law Enforcement Training Academy in Glynco, Georgia, graduating as class president. Jack has extensive military and law enforcement training, and is world traveled through his past military service. He resides in California where he is pursuing acting.::Computer Child', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jack Mahrt');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6429697', 'Constantine Malahias is an actor and writer, known for Hamlet in the Golden Vale (2017), Un-Speak-Able (2018) and Howeds (2016).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Constantine Malahias');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2933059', 'Max Mangel is known for his work on MeatEater (2012), Apex Predator (2015) and The Mind of a Chef (2012).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Max Mangel');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3016743', 'Grant opened his heart to acting by performing in theater for most of his childhood and young adult life. After college, he enrolled into the New York Film Academy in Burbank California with Universal Studios. While attending, Grant not only began to improve his acting for film abilities but also his screenwriting talents, directing and video editing. Grant graduated with honors and was labeled by his N.Y.F.A. instructors as the leader of his class. After graduating, he has worked in the film industry for years under an assortment of titles: Actor, Director, Producer, Writer, and Double.::Mentor', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Grant Christopher Maquet');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3789602', 'Dan was born in Chicago, Illinois on May 12, 1989 and a few years later moved with his mother to Sarasota, Florida where he was raised. He attended Southside Elementary School, McIntosh Middle School, Sarasota Middle School and then finally graduated from the Sarasota County Technical Institute when he was 16 in 2005.While attending Southside Elementary School, he was encouraged and supported by his teachers and fellow students to hone his writing skills. During middle school he wrote his first feature-length screenplay at 14. After graduating high school, he pursued many options, including looking at various film schools, but finally decided at 18 to embark on a filmmaking career himself.At 18, he moved back to Chicago where he continues to live. He directed his first short film entitled "Wake" that year, in which he also co-wrote and co-produced. He is currently working on finishing his second short film entitled "Fallen".::DMB', 'Daniel', 'Marcus-Best', NULL, NULL, 'Dan Marcus');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('6922468', 'Branden Marlowe is an actor, known for The Dark Knight Rises (2012), Vampires (1986) and Men in Black 3 (2012).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Branden Marlowe');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4318570', 'Sean Martin was born on the 5th of April 2000 and recalls wanting to act since the tender age of two years old. This lively and eloquent youngster grew serious about acting at ten years old. His acting debut was as "Young Francisco" of Monsters Inside Me, an Animal Planet series. Martin''s career now includes roles in various College Humor spoofs, television shows such as Team Toon and Redrum and starring as "Damaso" in the film Sin Dolor, which premiered at Grauman''s Chinese Theatre. He is an athlete who conversely loves to play video games. Sean has won numerous Acting and Film awards such as "Best Supporting Actor" at the 2012 LA Movie Awards, Best Film credits at Hollyshorts for Sin Dolor and more. He has a huge passion for animals and started an organization called "Kids Adopt a Shelter" to help animals worldwide. Winner of numerous government citations and awards for his efforts helping animals. Sean Martin is also a Regional Winner of the 2012 & 2013 Kohl''s Cares Scholarship.::M.P', 'Sean Martin', 'Posner', NULL, NULL, 'Sean Martin');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2691318', 'Catya Maré is a multiple award winning composer, music producer and classical crossover violinist from Germany, who lived / worked in California from 2008 - 2015. She received her US green card based on her achievements in the musical field. Winner of Hollywood Music in Media Award, Billboard World Song Contest and USA Songwriting Competition. She occasionally works as an actress, while musical creation is her main occupation. Since May, 2015 she''s back in Germany.::Catya Mare', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Catya Maré');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5050562', 'Aaron T. Rudd is an actor and writer, known for Lopez (2016), Honestly, Honestly (2012) and Other People''s Children (2015).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Aaron T. Rudd');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2975829', 'Tyler Rumsey is known for his work on The Town (2010), Win Win (2011) and Cake Boss (2009).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Tyler Rumsey');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1580576', 'Raised in Baltimore, Maryland, London May began his acting career early in Baltimore''s renowned Children''s Theater Association. After a long break to pursue a burgeoning and successful music career, London returned to acting in 2010, studying improv at The iO West and classic theatre with Uranium Madhouse, where he made his 2014 Los Angeles stage debut in The Duchess Of Malfi. He has also co-starred in the pilot episode of Ron Howard''s The Great Escape, and Cold Sweat, a short directed by James Cameron''s DP Paul Babin. Since then London has been busy with roles on The Disney Channel, Discovery Channel, Oxygen Channel, TNT, as well as appearing in numerous films and stage productions (most recently in Saw director Darren L. Bousman''s The Tension Experience)Besides acting on screen and stage, London May is also a highly regarded musician, best known as drummer and bassist with legendary singer Glenn Danzig''s seminal goth punk group Samhain. During his long and continuing music career London''s playing has been featured on over 30 releases and he has performed with such popular artists as Tiger Army, Son Of Sam (with Davey Havok of AFI), Lol Tolhurst (of The Cure), Lee Ving (of FEAR), Pat Smear (Nirvana, Foo Fighters), Exene Cervenka (of X), Dag Nasty, Cold Cave, Reptile House, Jackass star Chris Pontius, and Distorted Pony. In 2016 Cleopatra Records released Devilution: The Early Years, a deluxe retrospective CD/LP of London''s earliest recordings and in 2017 he joined the legendary Black Metal group, Ritual.::J. Patel', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'London May');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4255572', 'Mike J. McAllister was born on October 21, 1988 in Erie, Pennsylvania, USA as Michael John McAllister. He is an editor and actor, known for 1-900 (2011), Spill: The Reel Deal (2010) and Candy Cane Lane (2009).::Anonymous', 'Michael John', 'McAllister', '1988-10-21', NULL, 'Mike J. McAllister');
