INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2364305', 'John has appeared in over 250 commercials and industrials in the Southeast. He can also be seen in short films from 2000-2013 from UNCSA, Elon University, NC School of Communications Arts & Sciences.(November 2010) As an executive producer on smaller projects, John has completed six short documentaries and PSAs including the Outreach Program for the Delta County Schools, the WFU Campus Kitchen promotional video and the Turnaround Groups Web campaign. John frequently directs web content for Fear of Phobias, Q - Theory and Mischief Cinema.John is currently working on pre-production for his film series, The Darling Matter, which is set to begin production in 2014. John will write and direct, along with others, the four films in this original take on found footage and assembled footage movies. This film series will be co-produced by Mischief Cinema and Fear of Phobias, Film Co.John is a passionate advocate for legal and social issues and is frequently a part of campaigns in North Carolina involving extreme sentencing and prisoners rights.John is producing and directing with his partner, Suzanne Bauer, a series of movies for their company Mischief Cinema about four distinct legal controversies; The Felony Murder Doctrine, Restraining Orders, Plea Bargaining and Child Support Court in America. The first film is being produced under the guidelines of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences guidelines for award contention in 2016.(2007) John was a production assistant and featured extra on the Academy Award winning short, Two Soldiers.John has appeared in more than 300 short films.(July 2004) In 2004, John completed his first spec television pilot, Whistle Grove, the night before his daughter, Gretchen was born.(June 2006) John wrote and directed the experimental feature thriller, Scelerophobia, using a Canon home video camera and a cellphone camera in 2006.(1998) John was a finalist for the Chesterfield Writer''s film Project.(2014) John is competing for the Nicholl Fellowship in Screenwriting (Academy of Motion Picture Arts 7 Sciences) with his script, Everything''s Better with Sandy B. The script is a comedy fantasy take on a writer''s fictional relationship with one of America''s favorite Actresses in the aftermath of his divorce and the parental kidnapping of his daughter.::John Lawson', 'John Walter', 'Lawson', NULL, NULL, 'John Lawson');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2545052', 'Jean-Christophe Leger is an actor and cinematographer, known for Inception (2010), Born Without a Beat: The Journey of a Deaf Raver (2009) and Robin Hood (2010).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jean-Christophe Leger');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0939703', 'Frank Wood was born in 1960 in the USA. He is an actor, known for Changeling (2008), Michael Clayton (2007) and The Royal Tenenbaums (2001).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Frank Wood');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2411840', 'Benjamin Riley was born in New Orleans, Louisiana and was raised in Boston and New Jersey, before finally settling down with his family in Chicago. After deciding to pursue acting professionally in 2006 he was cast in 3 short films almost immediately. Four months into his career he was cast in Zack Parker Quench (2007). He Co-Starred in the dark drama opposite Bo Barrett and Mia Moretti. Quench (2007) was accepted into the New York International Independent Film and Video Festival and premiered on Sunset Blvd in Hollywood, CA in October 2007. Quench (2007) went on to win the coveted Best Director for a Feature Film award. Benjamin went on to do over 20 independent films ranging from shorts to features in a little over a year in the Midwest area with actors including Scott Ganyo, Steve ''Papaw'' Pyatte, D. Shane Christopher and Jim Dougherty in some of the films. After leaving college at Indiana University one semester shy of graduating and turning down a full ride scholarship to law school he moved to Los Angeles where he was cast in the starring role of a TV pilot 5 weeks after arriving. Currently he is attending the Howard Fine Acting Studio in Hollywood while being coached by legendary acting coach Howard Fine himself. He retained full representation within 3 months of moving to Los Angeles and is currently on the fast track to being a top actor among the who''s who of Young Hollywood.::Anonymous', 'Benjamin Riley', 'Schmitt', '1984-08-14', NULL, 'Benjamin Riley');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0757955', 'Norman Saleet has been a songwriter for well over 20 years. He has written hits for Air Supply "Here I am" & the late Selena "Where Did The Feeling Go?". He has worked with other artists such as Johnny Mathis, Art Garfunkel, Debbie Boone, Barry White, etc. He currently resides in Southern California with his wife, Judy and his daughter, Abbey. He is pursing acting and has starred in two national commercials, "Blue Shield" & "American Cancer Society". He also goes under the name Normand Scott Parish.::Abbey Scott', 'Norman', 'Sallitt', NULL, NULL, 'Norman Saleet');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4195263', 'Colin Smith is an actor, known for Evocator (2009) and Inception (2010).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Colin Smith');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3934065', 'Affan Tareen is an actor and assistant director, known for Inception (2010), Fortress (2012) and Ivy League Romance (2010).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Affan Tareen');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0498023', 'Philip holds a Bachelor of Arts in Directing from the College of Arts at Nihon University in Japan, a Diploma in Management of Executive Development from the Chinese University of Hong Kong, a Master of Fine Arts in Producing from The American Film Institute (AFI), and a Doctorate in Business Administration from Hong Kong Polytechnic University. He was the recipient of The Mary Pickford Foundation Scholarship at AFI. From 1987 to 1993, Philip ran the Production Department at Salon Films Hong Kong. While at Salon Films, he was the Asian unit production manager on more than 20 Hollywood films and numerous television productions, including Dragon - The Bruce Lee Story, M. Butterfly and Around the World in Eighty Days (TV Series). After returning to Asia in 1996 from his studies in the United States, Philip received Associate Producer or Line Producer credits in successful feature films such as CHEN Kaige''s The Emperor and the Assassin, Ang Lee''s Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon, Zhang Yimou''s Hero, Ronny Yu''s Fearless, Jan de Bont''s Lara Croft Tomb Raider: The Cradle of Life (Hong Kong Unit), and Rob Minkoff''s Forbidden Kingdom. In 2008, he line produced the Hong Kong portion of Chris Nolan''s The Dark Knight. Most recently, he executive produced Tom Tykwer and the Wachowskis'' Cloud Atlas, which is based on David Mitchell''s best seller. This is the most expensive independent film of all time with most of equity investment from Asia. In 2007 Philip Lee set up Javelin Pictures, a production company based in Beijing, with a view to producing viable cross-cultural film projects.::16thSIFF', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Philip Lee');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0350454', 'Academy Award-nominated actress Maggie Gyllenhaal was born on November 16, 1977, on the Lower East Side of Manhattan in New York City. Her parents, Naomi Foner (née Achs) and Stephen Gyllenhaal, are both filmmakers, and her brother is actor Jake Gyllenhaal. Her mother is from an Ashkenazi Jewish family, while her father has Swedish, English, Swiss-German, and German ancestry.Maggie made her film debut in Stephen''s film Waterland (1992). She had sporadic roles throughout her teenage years, though she stepped away to receive a degree in literature from Columbia University in 1999. In addition, she studied briefly at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Arts in London, which helped with her post-graduation transition back in to acting.Soon after graduation, Gyllenhaal appeared in supporting roles in A morte Hollywood (2000) and alongside brother Jake Gyllenhaal in Donnie Darko (2001). Her breakout role came a bit later, when she took on the daring, sexy title role in Secretary (2002). That part wound up earning her a Golden Globe nomination, and Gyllenhaal followed that up with supporting turns in 40 Days and 40 Nights (2002), Confessions of a Dangerous Mind (2002), Adaptation. (2002), and Mona Lisa Smile (2003), among other movies.Gyllenhaal received her second Golden Globe nomination for playing a recent prison parolee in Sherrybaby (2006). She followed that up with roles in World Trade Center (2006) and Stranger Than Fiction (2006), and then replaced Katie Holmes in the role of Rachel Dawes in The Dark Knight (2008).In 2009, Gyllenhaal received great acclaim for her role opposite Jeff Bridges in Crazy Heart (2009), which earned the actress her first Oscar nomination. Since then, Gyllenhaal has been seen in Nanny McPhee Returns (2010), Hysteria (2011) and Won''t Back Down (2012).Gyllenhaal has two children with husband Peter Sarsgaard, whom she married in 2009.::Anonymous and Bee', 'Margaret Ruth', 'Gyllenhaal', '1977-11-16', NULL, 'Maggie Gyllenhaal');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5207628', 'Mary Stifflemire is an actress, known for Bernie (2011) and Cell Phone Opera (2013).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mary Stifflemire');
