INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8479764', 'Deonte DelShon Stubbs, second to oldest child of eight children born and raised in Warren, Ohio by Veronica W. Lacey and Free L. Stubbs (1974-1999).Deonte, also known as Tae, grew a love for the performing arts watching Michael Jackson and Usher, then in 2005 as Chris Brown made an appearance on television. The love that grew for dance from being inspired by Chris Brown after the release of "Run It" sparked his leadership characteristic and started his dance group in his community. Performing talent shows and winning all over Trumbull county, Stubbs later then went solo as a performer. Cleveland Cavaliers Scream Team and America''s Got Talent were not the answer as a single dancer but Teyana Taylor''s "Undercover" music video (2016) was a great fit for him. He earned a role with the famous singer/actress as a lead dancer. From that point forward, his career in the performing arts became the ultimate priority.Stubbs became the bigger inspiration in the community leading with acting roles in Surviving Compton (2016) as a Death Row member. Gaining his first appearance on television, the success continued with appearances in commercials with Giant Eagle (2016) as a worker. As time went on, Stubbs took advantage of time and kept rising in the community and in the production world.In 2017, he took on his first major speaking role as an actor in an independent film directed by James Madio, "Use of Force" as Maze. Joining forces with north-eastern casting companies, he continued with acting. Deonte earned a role in "Pitch Perfect 3" (2017) as military personnel and Intel commercial with LeBron James (2017) as a photographer and crowd respondent. Later became partnered with Sony Productions in an upcoming film with Matthew McConaughey (2017) as a featured gang member relative. Stretching from films hitting movie theaters, Netflix became a part of Deonte''s resume with "Little Evil" (2017) as a crowd respondent.Stubbs is rising to the top as an inspired actor and performer. Tae creates his own short films in his hometown and writes plays for high schools to perform and spreads the wealth of expressing yourself through the performing arts.::Deonte Stubbs', NULL, NULL, '1991-10-16', NULL, 'Deonte Stubbs');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('9129819', 'Arai is an actress, known for White Boy Rick (2018).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Arai');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8318837', 'Laura Allen is an actress from Cleveland, Ohio and began her career in the 1970''s while attending Ohio State University, where she was majoring in broadcast journalism. In Hawaii, where she lived for almost 20 years, Laura continued to do print work and background and was cast in Aaron Spelling''s 1980 TV Pilot Waikiki starring Donna Mills and Dak Rambo. After returning to Cleveland and raising her son, she resumed her acting career mainly due to the influx of TV and Film opportunities that became available in the Cleveland area. From May 2015 to May 2017, Laura was a featured background actor in several feature films including The Land (High School Principal) In Search of Fellini (Catholic Nun) Aftermath (TV Reporter) The Fast and The Furious (Business Woman) The Bye Bye Man (Train Inspector) and Dog Eat Dog (Grocery Shopper). She also had a supporting role as the mother of a troubled teen in an independent thriller called The Colours of Desire (2017) and a re-occurring role as the girlfriend of a mob boss in the local crime Web Series entitled The Connected (2017).::Laura Allen', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Laura Allen');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('8900336', 'Gregory S. Anderson is an actor, known for Legacy (2017) and White Boy Rick (2018).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Gregory S. Anderson');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('7839054', 'Victoria was born in Warren, OH, to Jonathan and Pauline Watkins. She moved to Columbus, OH in 2002. She has a Nursing degree.She is married to Donald Borbridge, and has five children. Her husband is from Sitka, AK.Victoria has been acting, dancing and singing as soon as she could walk.::Victoria Borbridge', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Victoria Borbridge');
