INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('7527301', 'Valeria Vallejos is an Argentinian-French actress of Spanish decent, born and raised in Patagonia Argentina. She left Patagonia for Paris, France at the age of 17 to pursue her career in the arts. After brief study in Paris, Valeria went on to travel the world extensively continuing her education in the arts, mastering 3 languages and collecting an MBA along the way. Valeria has appeared in the films Concussion(2015), Live By Night(2016), landed the lead role of Camilla in the critically acclaimed short The Impossible Joy and will be featured as Angel in the upcoming indy film Lost Fare. Currently and permanently based in Los Angeles, she is an up and coming Latin tour de force.::Brett Reed', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Valeria Vallejos');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4737716', 'Sam Vanivray is an actor and writer, known for Enough to Be Dangerous (2015), Brute Sanity (2017) and Bracelet Instinct (2017).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sam Vanivray');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4075365', 'Having earned an MFA degree in Acting from the University of California~Davis, Phillip E. Walker has more than a half century of experience in "The Industry". Having just ended his first LA season with 133 shoots, his "Entry Level Acting in LA" hands on full employment manual for actors releases Sept. 29, 2015. Fortunate enough to have never accepted a job outside of his field since graduating college, that Loyola University of Chicago renaissance man training helped PhilE build a diverse arts career including: multiple university theatre professorships throughout America such as chairing the Fisk University Speech & Drama Department; several arts administration positions such as the first ever California Arts Council Arts Touring Coordinator; creator/leader of more than ten (10) youth summer arts camps including SummerCampCalifornia; plus full time stints with several theatre companies such as collective membership in the TONY Award winning San Francisco Mime Troupe. With more than four (400) hundred live theatrical productions under his belt, Phillip has also directed many plays. Blessed with having had the best parents in the world, Walker was taught to be a "professional traveler". Among the fruits of that upbringing was his becoming founding Artistic Director of the African American Drama Company, a Black History theatre in its 39th season which has performed at least twice in every United State. Mr. Walker''s only son (City Solar Regional Manager Travis Donnell Walker) has given birth to a daughter Aliah Janae Walker.::self', 'Phillip Eugene', 'Walker', NULL, NULL, 'Phillip E. Walker');
