INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4005193', 'Pennie Marie became popular taking on the role of Officer J. Caliendo in AMC Televisions "Low Winter Sun" produced by Chris Mundy. Off screen Pennie Marie is a runway and trade-show model. In her earliest years Pennie began absorbing her acting career in Mosiac Theater and undertook classes at Gordan Michaels Studios. As a member of the Glee club she performed in various stage productions at Detroit Music Hall and the Masonic Temple. Her exotic look derives from her mixed ancestry of Italian, French Canadian, African-American, Irish, Cherokee, and Egyptian.In the early 2000''s Pennie was cast in various small films such as "Red and Blue Marbles, "Born of Earth", and "After The Blood Rush. Pennies acclaim increased after her Reoccuring role in season 1 of ABC''S Detroit 187 as a Uniformed Cop. She was inspired to advance her acting after working with Carmen Ejogo as Child Protective Service worker in Alex Cross and Body Doubling Carmen Ejogo in the remake of Sparkle. Pennie''s costarring role in Ironcore Media''s Necroland as Cor Thia Burgeon was her acclaim to her leading role of Alena, the wife of D12''s Swift Mcvay in Count Time.::Pennie Marie Hawkins', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Pennie-Marie Hawkins');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4103946', 'Ron Heisler is known for his work on The Five-Year Engagement (2012), The Hunger Games: Catching Fire (2013) and Freaky Deaky (2012).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ron Heisler');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5831016', 'Sarah Hess was born on August 8th to Charlie & Teresa Hess, née Fryman, at Travis Air Force Base in Fairfield, California on her mother''s birthday. During Hess''s early childhood, her family moved between San Diego, San Francisco, & Modesto. Once her father''s service was completed in the U.S. Navy, Charlie & Teresa relocated the family to Cincinnati, OH where her parents originated. As she grew up, Hess discovered her dream for performing arts early on, declaring she was going to become an actress and make movies. Her dream for California remained and she vowed to return to live there again. During middle school and high school, Hess began acting in theater productions. Later, Hess attended Miami University for film production & photography, becoming highly proficient working both sides of the camera. It was at Miami that Hess got her first taste of life on set of a large scale production after she got a call from her mother about a background casting call for Disney''s Secretariat filming in Louisville, KY. A short time later, The Ides of March came to her very own campus & Hess didn''t hesitate to answer the casting call. There was no turning back from this pivotal moment. Hess changed her major to Film Production and began honing her knowledge and creative outlets in order to fuel her dream in the Industry. To date, Hess''s talents vastly range between acting, modeling, performing music on vocals/guitar/piano, dance, multimedia art, special effects makeup, production crew, & most importantly, people. Her true passion has continued to burn on, driving her to what is now a promising future in film. Hess continues her quest through challenging roles that tap into the human psyche.::Sarah Hess', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sarah Hess');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4262936', 'Kimberly Koltyk is a Ukrainian American actress born and raised in the Metro Detroit area. Coming from a family of working musicians, that was her family''s focus for her at a young age, playing Clarinet for many years as well as chorus, and dabbling a bit with the guitar as well with her father as her teacher. But she knew from a very young age, that as much as she loved music and wanted to follow in the footsteps of her family, acting and movies were really where her heart was. Watching all the old teen comedy''s, especially anything John Hughes, or John Waters. Loving the feeling of living vicariously through her favorite characters. She went many years without pursuing her dream, due to a lack of knowledge into the industry etc.Until about 4 years ago, when she took a trip to Wilmington, NC to see filming locations, production studios and even watch a episode of her favorite TV show being filmed right in the small town of Wilmington. It was at that very moment that it hit her, that if they could do it in such a small town, why not in Detroit? Life is too short to not chase your dreams. The day she got back to Michigan she enrolled herself into acting classes, signed on with a agency & a few extras casting directors, and it was right around then that Michigan passed the 42% tax incentive, it was as if it were a meant to be. She has been non stop ever since, getting to meet many cool Celebritys as well as make some very cool connections and friends along the journey.She would like to take this as far as she can, and hopes to keep the film industry alive here in Michigan and would like to one day move to California. She has a huge admiration for David Lynch and all his film work.::Kimberly Koltyk', NULL, NULL, '1982-02-26', NULL, 'Kimberly Koltyk');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0356501', 'Jen Halley was born in 1971. She is an actress and producer, known for Red Riding Hood (2011), Battlestar Galactica (2004) and Sarah in the Dark (2008).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jen Halley');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4004498', 'Olivia Steele Falconer is an actress, known for Red Riding Hood (2011), The Client List (2010) and Crowsnest (2012).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Olivia Steele Falconer');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5100155', 'Since graduating from Miami University with a BA in theatre (''11), Jon founded Cincinnati''s Unity Productions, helped build Untethered Theatre Co. (''12-''13), became an Associate Artist at Know Theatre (''14-''15), and has worked with internationally recognized film-makers (George Clooney, Andy Goddard), authors (Nic Balthazar, Ron Jones), and theaters (Playhouse in the Park, Human Race). Receiving awards and critical acclaim as an actor, musician, director, writer, and producer, Jon continues to expand on his career in the arts.::Jon Kovach', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jon Kovach');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4357749', 'Abe Larkin is known for his work on One Night Alone, The Citizen (2012) and The Ides of March (2011).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Abe Larkin');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4030500', 'Kef Lee is known for his work on The Secret Village (2013), Waterfront Nightmare (2012) and The Citizen (2012). He has been married to Mary since August 12, 1989. They have three children.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Kef Lee');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4309285', 'Linda joined the thousands of Michiganders who benefited from Governor Jennifer Granholm''s generous Film Tax Incentive that brought Hollywood activity to her native state of Michigan in 2008. She was fortunate to see some of the best directors, producers, and crews during the early years of filming. Having been raised in immigrant communities and attending 11 schools by the age of 15, she learned acting as a survival mechanism, but had no formal training. Being a naturalized American citizen, she has dual British and American nationality. Having lived in three countries and three geographically diverse regions in America has added to her repertoire of characters that she can portray. Among the many accents she is familiar with and can reproduce is French, Scottish, Geordi, Cockney, German, Italian, Spanish, Southern, Midwestern and Southwestern USA. She is good at imitating a wide variety of animals and age brackets, having a three and a half octave vocal range. If one type of sound doesn''t fit, she can step into the character of another one. Married, mother of three grown children, grandmother and running a small farm on 13 acres in the country, she lives one day at a time, enjoying whatever life may bring across her path. Linda was born in Sarnia, Ontario to John and Sheila Box, along with her older sister Connie, all of whom had immigrated to Canada in 1952. The family immigrated to America in 1959, the first home being in Battle Creek, Michigan. John Box worked on Grand Trunk Railroad and moved his family frequently in search of a better position in the company. He formed three bicycle clubs in Michigan, and his two daughters raced with top honours in the sixties. Both parents have since passed away, leaving Linda and her sister as lone survivors of the legacy of their parents. Linda resides in the Greater Lansing Area in Mid-Michigan with her husband, Ed Linsley, their family and his extended family. Her location is central to Michigan Films being between the two major film municipalities of Grand Rapids and Detroit.::Lindy Lee', 'Linda Jean', 'Box', NULL, NULL, 'Linda Linsley');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4488076', 'Michael Loos is a film/TV actor/producer/voice-over talent who grew up imitating scenes on TV, then acted in his high school drama club. He came to love the instant feedback from the audience in live performances. He especially loved doing comedies because of the joy they brought the audience. Because he loves to see people smile, he soon became the life of the party almost everywhere he went.But his passion for acting never ceased. Michael acted in church plays and short dramas before eventually beginning to work through an agent for commercial, industrial and film work. Michael is a film actor, but works on commercials, industrials and stage plays between films helps him stay sharp. MichaelAs a producer, Michael is focused on creating original content that forces the audience to form their own own opinions about the storyline. He constantly has 3-5 projects in the different stages of production, from development to post-production.::Heather Salisbury', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Michael Loos');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('4759629', 'Norine Marsh was born as Norine Hope Racklin. She is known for her work on The Ides of March (2011), People Who Hurt (2014) and Goodbye Walt (2012).::Anonymous', 'Norine Hope', 'Racklin', NULL, NULL, 'Norine Marsh');
