INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2139388', 'Originally from Perth, Western Australia, Elliott attended Hale Private Boys School. His passion was playing baseball for the state level competition. He decided to make the move to Sydney and beyond to further his love and aspirations of playing professional baseball. His passion for the game took him to the USA on and off for a few years working as a camp counselor until it was time to leave the game.In 2007, Elliott picked up various projects including the lead role in a Volvo sponsored TVC for the Asthma Foundation, directed by Marc Furmie. It was definitely a confidence booster & may be the stepping stone for a positive move forward in the acting life.2009 become a year of self-development and self-promotion, producing & fully financing a short film called Denouement, written by Peter R Kirk. It garnered several awards such as Best International Film at the Southern California Film Festival in 2009, Best Drama at the West Hollywood International Film Festival in 2009 and Honorary Awards at several other festivals around the globe.Since then, Elliott has appeared in many TV series, films, short films and TVC''s including The Secret Daughter (2016), Here Come the Habibs! (2016), Rake (2010), the hit US crime show Deadly Women (2008), Redfern Now: Stand Up (2012) and Crownies: Episode #1.10 (2011) to name a few.Lately, Elliott has been actively producing and writing his own projects, working with screenwriter Jennifer Harrison on the feature film ''Revelations''.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1979-08-28', NULL, 'Elliott Collinson');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5536718', 'Ryan was born in Port Moresby Papua New Guinea to an Australian missionary family. His father traveled through PNG, Vanuatu, Australia and New Zealand. After high-school in Auckland New Zealand, Ryan fought competitively in Tae kwon do and won 2 tournaments. He worked as a Carpenter for six years and was brought to New York in 2008 to featured in the DKNY Jeans campaign with Bahati Prinsloo. His rugged good looks landing him in campaigns for Armani Exchange with Izabel Goulart, Abercrombie and Fitch, Hugo Boss underwear, Trussardi Jeans and Esprit underwear with Gisele Bundchen and Erin Wasson. He''s been seen in TV commercials around the globe for brands such as Paramount pictures, Rock Port, Garnier, Macy''s, A+F and Just Jeans.Since fashion Ryan is making strides into leading man territory onscreen, playing Jake Bolin the "Flirtual Killer" on MTV''s EYE CANDY and will be seen JUNE 2017 in "ROCK THAT BODY" opposite Scarlett Johansson and Kate McKinnon. Ryan will also be seen playing OWEN in the NY TIMES best selling adaptation of CONFESS, written and directed by Elissa Down out March 2017. Ryan continues to build his body of work spending time writing, directing and developing skills in all areas of the film world. His short film "Left Behind" is about the confrontation between a mother struggling with her depression and a son''s unorthodox methods to help her see reason. It was inspired by the loss of loved ones and in an effort to raise awareness for those suffering with mental illnesses and depression. Ryan continues to work alongside Susan Batson and Anthony Meindl as he explores characters in his writing and grows as an artist. (Bio by: Michael Rex Hooker)::Michael Rex Hooker', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ryan Cooper');
