INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1705074', 'Sohm Kapila was raised in Nottinghamshire. At the age of 16 Sohm was picked to join the Central Television Workshop and later moved to London to classically train as an Actress. Sohm studied film acting further in New York, and comedy sitcom in Los Angeles and now resides here in LA. Sohm has worked alongside director Alex Kurtzman in her first blockbuster film The Mummy. She also looks forward to the release of Love Type D directed by Sasha Collington. Her TV experience in England includes the 50th live episode of Coronation Street for ITV, Casualty, Paradox, Waking the Dead and Doctors for the BBC. She was also one of the regular voices in the award winning radio soap - Silver Street, for the BBC Asian Network for 6 years. Between Film and TV roles, Sohm loves to work on the stage, sing and write, and has been in over 20 Stage productions around the world and also on the WestEnd working with Sonia Friedman Productions in Bend It Like Beckham the Musical which was nominated for five Olivier Awards in 2015 and Sohm was consequently nominated for Best Featured Actress and Best understudy with the WhatsonStage Awards. Her self produced, co-written film - The Problem with Kaldeep, was recently selected for the London Indian Film Festival 2017.::Aim Agents', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sohm Kapila');
