INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2917955', 'Adrian Nanney was born in Roanoke Virginia. After moving around a lot as a kid, Adrian''s family settled in Fredericksburg, Virginia.As a young man Adrian was diagnosed with dyslexia and learned at an early age how to overcome adversity. At the age of 19 Adrian started taking a major interest in the acting & modeling industries. He started off as a model and then got into acting. He had two great influences in the industry; Mike Tyminski, Photographer and founder of Mike''s Portraits, an inspirational man who introduced Adrian to the world of acting, and Denny O''Rourke, a local actor, who helped guide Adrian in the right direction.Adrian''s first movie was Step Up 2: The Streets (2008), directed by Jon M. Chu and was cast as an extra, "Dragon Club Patron". His first appearance on camera was in Border Town (2009), directed by Chris Alan Williams, in which he appeared as a "Featured Thug". Later he was cast in Spielberg''s award winning historical drama Lincoln (2012), as an extra, credited as "Union Soldier" and as Daniel Day Lewis''s stand-in, who played the titular role. It was, in short, an amazing opportunity. Adrian''s first significant role was in Legends & Lies: The Real West (Episode 1, 2015) directed by Kevin Hershberger. Based upon the book by Bill O''Reilly, in the supporting role of "Charlie Ford", one of Jesse James gang members. The independent film by Russ Fulmore, The Edge Of Time (2016), Adrian played the role of "Talon", a Time Traveler.::Adrian Nanney', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Adrian Nanney');
