INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5785582', 'Born and raised in Sydenham England, but now resides in North West London.Collet is trained in the filmmaking/Arts and volunteering sectors with over a decade of experience in film.She is an award wining film Producer and has a Skillset Media Academy Bachelors Film Degree from Middlesex University.She has worked in several different departments in film and film production including Management, Producing and distribution.She also has a rather large interest in multiple business ownership and online startups.Collet has trained with and supported the Prince''s Trust and has obtained her Level II Enterprise Award. And now runs two businesses one of them helping student filmmakers getting film internships.::www.mise-en-scene.co.uk', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Collet Collins');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2583910', 'Fiona Dwyer was born in Dublin, Ireland. She first fell in love with the theatre when she was cast as Titania in Shakespeare''s "A Midsummer Night''s Dream" at age sixteen. She then went on to study drama at Trinity College, Dublin and at The Dublin Oscar Theatre School where she met her future husband actor/writer/director Shay Dunphy.::Marie Jaffe', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Fiona Dwyer');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0687964', 'Jeremy Podeswa was born in 1962 in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. He is a director, known for Game of Thrones (2011), Boardwalk Empire (2010) and Fugitive Pieces (2007).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jeremy Podeswa');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('0638354', 'David Nutter was born in 1960 in the USA. He is a director and producer, known for Generazione perfetta (1998), The X-Files (1993) and Game of Thrones (2011). He has been married to Birgit Nutter since May 1987. They have two children.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'David Nutter');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3439870', 'Born in France, Eric Geynes is of English/French parentage. In 2003, he relocated to London from Toulouse following a career in professional swimming. He trained at Drama Centre London (Colin Firth, Paul Bettany, Lambert Wilson, Pierce Brosnam). Following graduation, rather than waiting for roles, he wrote and acted in the short film Unspoken, awarded Best Digital Film in Sao Paulo. He has acted on stage in numerous productions, from Berkoff''s Metamorphosis to Sarah Kane''s Blasted. He is trained in unarmed stage fighting (Alison de Burgh) and rides regularly at the Mudchute Equestrian Centre. He now works and lives between London and Paris.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Eric Geynes');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3660294', 'Mitch Hill is known for his work on Quizmaster (2012), Ten (2013) and Jack the Giant Slayer (2013).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mitch Hill');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3450504', 'Carl Marino was born and raised in upstate New York in the city of Hornell, the son of Carl and Carol Marino. He was the only boy of four siblings. After graduation from High School, Carl attended the United States Military Academy at West Point for 2 years. Following West Point, and while studying Criminal Justice at the Rochester Institute of Technology, Carl became a Deputy Sheriff in New York and served for almost 17 years on the force. He also signed with a modeling company in NY and worked on print and commercial projects. After his service and the passing of both of his parents, Carl moved to California to be closer to some of his family that had moved there years before. While in California, He signed with a modeling agency there. Soon after his arrival, he auditioned for a feature film, got the part, and made his big screen debut in the independent film Sedona''s Rule (2010). Almost immediately after this, he was cast in the NBC show "Trauma" (2009)_ that was filming in San Francisco, and became a recurring guest star. Since then, Carl has worked on and been featured in numerous feature films, network and cable television shows, and national commercials. He is most well known for portraying the lead Detective, Lt. Joe Kenda, on the Investigation Discovery hit TV show "Homicide Hunter: Lt. Joe Kenda" for 7 seasons. Carl lives in San Francisco and works between there, Los Angeles, New York, and the Southeast. He is married to Ilona Marino and has two adult children from a previous marriage.::Carl Marino', 'Carl Earl', 'Marino', '1970-08-26', NULL, 'Carl Marino');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3593624', 'Ilona Marino is an actress, known for Anjaana Anjaani (2010), Contractor''s Routine (2011) and Il mio nome è Khan (2010). She has been married to Carl Marino since August 28, 2010.::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ilona Marino');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3676214', 'Chloe Page is an actress and producer, known for Sweeney Todd: The Demon Barber of Fleet Street (2007), The Woman in Black (2012) and One Day (2011).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Chloe Page');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2936003', 'Sarah-Jane Paige is an actress, known for Hereafter (2010), Dead Cat (2013) and How to Lose Friends & Alienate People (2008).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Sarah-Jane Paige');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2425695', 'Wine Oh TV Founder and Host Monique Soltani is a seasoned journalist with a Bachelor of Arts in Broadcast Journalism and American Studies and well over a decade of experience working as a broadcaster. Most recently, you may have seen Monique reporting on weather and wine for The Weather Channel. Monique honed her reporting skills working at television stations across the country including: KPIX-TV/CBS 5, KNTV-TV/NBC 11, KSEE-TV/NBC 24, KCBS-TV/CBS 2, KGTV-TV/ABC 10, and KPVI-TV/NBC 6. She has a certification from the Court of Master Sommeliers, is an experienced wine judge, and has interviewed at least two hundred winemakers, dozens of top chefs, and A-list celebrities like Jennifer Lawrence, Nicole Kidman and Kate Hudson. Monique is also a trained SAG/AFTRA actor and studied at The Groundlings, Warner Loughlin Studios and The Atlantic Theater Company and she can be seen on various films, television shows and commercials. Monique is passionate about telling people''s stories and created Wine Oh TV to share her love of wine, journalism and television with the world. For over five years Monique has been covering the wine scene in California and around the world. While she has extensive experience covering wine, food and travel she''s no three trick pony. Monique has covered a variety of "beats" in the broadcasting business including: Courts and Crime, Breaking News, Health & Fitness, Entertainment, Traffic, and yes even a little Weather.::Suzy Sherman', 'Shainne Monique', 'Soltani', '1975-12-03', NULL, 'Monique Soltani');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2512552', 'Brian Vowell was born on December 19, 1975 in Loring AFB, Maine, USA. He is known for his work on Milk (2008), The Kite Runner (2007) and Hereafter (2010).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1975-12-19', NULL, 'Brian Vowell');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2339366', 'Paul Warren is a British actor known for playing characters in prosthetic makeup and creature suits in such films as Star Wars: The Force Awakens, Guardians of the Galaxy, Thor: The Dark World, Clash of the Titans and World War Z.He began his film career as a body double for Daniel Radcliffe on the film Harry Potter & the Order of the Phoenix. Spending much of his time 20ft up in the air on the hydraulic broomstick system and performing other physically demanding activities, it wasn''t long before Paul started to get noticed as a versatile performer.In 2007, he was recommended to the legendary Stan Winston Studio as a good choice to portray an emaciated version of the title character in ''The Deaths of Ian Stone''. The horror role required full body prosthetics and cgi head replacement with lead actor Mike Vogel. The invaluable experience Paul gained working with Stan''s crew to achieve this tricky effect is what ultimately set him on a path to becoming a creature performer.His first creature role was in the remake of Clash of the Titans. Working with the Oscar nominated Creatures Inc, he underwent a 5 hour makeup process to transform into a tortured soul that pulls the boatman across the river styx. To add to the challenge of performing covered in such extreme silicone prosthetics, the scene was filmed in a large outside water tank at Pinewood studios.In 2010, Paul was chosen by director Joe Johnston to be a visual effect double for skinny Steve Rogers in Captain America: The First Avenger. Working closely with Lola Visual Effects, he helped bring Skinny Steve to life in the pre-production VFX tests and was on set as a visual reference for the recruitment scene. The remainder of body double duties on the film were performed by Leander Deeny and Paul went on to work on X-Men: First Class.He has since gone on to appear in many films playing aliens and monsters, but most notably in Star Wars: The Force Awakens along side Neal Scanlan''s CFX crew. Paul is credited as a ''creature and droid puppeteer'' and he plays an alien called ''Varmik''. This character is of particular interest to Star Wars fans due to his origin and connection to the original trilogy. Varmik is based on 2 classic pieces of Ralph McQuarrie production art from 1975 - the cantina showdown and early Chewbacca designs. The former was a particular favourite of J.J Abrams'' that he wanted to bring to life on screen.::anonymous', NULL, NULL, '1974-10-28', NULL, 'Paul Warren');
