INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1879820', 'Jayk is an actor, producer, director, screenwriter... plus musician, band booker, comedian, host, rapper, poet, teacher, radio personality, event coordinator, among other things.April 2017 Jayk will appear as an actor on HBO''s Emmy award winning "Veep", but he''s best known for his role in the film "The Social Network". He also appeared in the Coen Brothers'' "Hail Cesar!" as well as on CBS, TNT, MTV, ABC Family, Comedy Central, E!, The Disney Channel, and other networks in shows like CSI: NY, SouthLAnd, Crash and Bernstein and many others. He stars as Brandon Dedd in the feature "Dedd Brothers" now available on Amazon and Netflix. Jayk has appeared in over 40 national commercials. imdb.me/jaykJayk arrived in LA in 2004 after graduating from Emerson College with a degree in Acting and Directing, and has trained at North Carolina School of the Arts, Boston University Theater Institute, and El Galliner in Girona, Spain. Jayk has performed stand-up comedy regularly at The Comedy Store, The Improv Hollywood, The Ha Ha Comedy Club etc.As a writer-producer, he has created and sold series of comedic content to Current TV, Fremantle Media, Sun Microsystems, among others. Jayk also produced several hip-hop and indie rock music videos, called "a kick to the gut" by SPIN Magazine, and "breathtaking" by The Huffington Post, among other praise from national press outlets.Recently, Jayk produced the magical realism short film "Synching" which starred ****** ******* (This Is Us, Silicon Valley, Love, AT&T''s "Lily"), Lauren Flans (Wild N Out, Another Period), Laurie Kirkpatrick (Conan O''Brien), Adam Gifford (Longmire, Wristcutters: A Love Story), Dan Bell (Wayne''s World I & II) etc, currently in festival consideration pending release. Directly after that, he directed and produced a music video for the song "Precious Gold" by Beca, which drops April 2017, and has been praised by such outlets as Stereogum, Flaunt Magazine, Lucky Magazine, and many others.Gallagher is currently in pre-production, associate producing and casting an Afghan War short called "Hajji" in association with David J Lawson of Snowfort Pictures (XX, Jodorowsky''s Dune), employing Stephen Spielberg''s production designer, the sound designer from The Matrix and Call Of Duty games, and starring Dayo Okeniyi (Shades of Blue).Jayk is a produced playwright, published poet, and a prolific screenwriter. He created several projects with Brimmer Street Theater Company''s Blueprint Series, workshopping "The Apprehension of Dr. Kaczynski" and "Synching," later transforming these projects into screenplays. Gallagher writes reviews for multiple travel websites, press releases for the theater, film and music industries, and has 12 years experience tutoring SAT English and Grammar.Gallagher''s grunge band Hobart W Fink has been called " "Imposing" by SPIN Magazine, and "Mosh-worthy" by CMJ. The band has debuted two singles on KROQ'' s Rodney on the ROQ, and played on over 100 stations nationwide. Songs have been placed in such cult hits as "Sharknado 2" and "Three Headed Shark Attack". Hobart W Fink''s last two releases were recorded by Chris Kasych (Wavves, Phantogram, Vampire Weekend, P!nk, Santigold) and mastered by Alex DeYoung (Macy Gray, NOFX, Pennywise). The most recent EP features guest vocals from Rachel Fox, former star of Desperate Housewives and current wunderkind futures trader. Hobart W Fink performed six shows at South By Southwest 2016, and has headlined festivals like Echo Park Rising, Make Music Pasadena, Venice Music Crawl, Buzzbands.la Chinatown Nights, plus rocked every indie venue in LA and most states in the country.Before the band started in 2012, Jayk released four rap EPs over two years. He participated in national battle league Grind Time, garnering over 100,000 views on YouTube videos of his intense battles in front of thousands of live spectators. Jayk directed plays in Los Angeles with needtheater and Brimmer Street Theater Company, and in Boston with Circle Theater Group.Jayk is a show promoter, running a band booking company and record label called All Scene Eye. ASE artists have played in heavy rotation on KCRW, KPFK, KROQ, KEDG and more top stations. ASE is frequently contracted to book stages for major nationwide festivals, and consistently books talent at many LA venues. You can hear Jayk every other Sunday on AM1630 KCHUNG playing local bands on All Scene Eye Radio.::Shane Carpenter', 'Jacob Patrick', 'Gallagher', NULL, NULL, 'Jayk Gallagher');
