INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2240346', 'Kodi was born on June 13, 1996 in Adelaide, Australia, to Sonja Smit and Andy McPhee, who is an actor and professional wrestler. His sister is actress Sianoa Smit-McPhee.In 2014, Kodi starred in Twentieth Century Fox''s Dawn of the Planet of the Apes opposite Andy Serkis, Jason Clarke, Gary Oldman, and Keri Russell. The project reunited him with director Matt Reeves with whom he previously worked with on the film Let Me in (opposite Chloe Moretz). The film has grossed over $700MM Worldwide.The film Young Ones (dir: Jake Paltrow) in which Kodi starred opposite Michael Shannon, Nicholas Hoult and Elle Fanning, premiered at the 2014 Sundance Film Festival.Kodi was recently at the 2015 Sundance Film Festival for the premiere of Slow West (dir. John MacLean), in which he stars opposite Michael Fassbender and Ben Mendelsohn. The film received the World Cinema Grand Jury Prize. It''s a Western two hander that takes place in the Wild West in the 1870''s. A24 has released the film in the US to rave reviews. Earlier in 2015, Kodi was seen as the lead role in an epic 8 part Australian television mini series Gallipoli (2015) (Channel Nine) based on the infamous WWI battle that took place 100 years ago.In 2016, Kodi co-starred in X-Men: Apocalypse (2016) (dir: Bryan Singer) for Twentieth Century Fox, portraying the role of Nightcrawler.He lives in Los Angeles.::MGMT. Entertainment', NULL, NULL, '1996-06-13', NULL, 'Kodi Smit-McPhee');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('3663151', 'Bob Dwyer is an actor, known for When in Rome (2010).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Bob Dwyer');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5330651', 'Hannah Barefoot was born in Cody, Wyoming, and was raised on classic films and backyard plays. She realized she wanted to be an actress, singer, and dancer when she first saw Rita Hayworth in the 1944 film, ''Cover Girl'', and has followed that dream ever since. She pursued a BFA at the nationally acclaimed Department of Theatre and Dance at the University of Wyoming where she studied acting, dancing, and vocal performance.After college, Hannah moved to Portland, OR, and took a few years off to reevaluate her life. When she finally returned to acting, she switched her emphasis from theatre to film and television. It was in Portland that she received her first TV credit, NBC''s "Grimm", developed her comedy and improvisational chops in "The ScreenPrinters" web series, and made a name for herself as a dramatic indie actress with a lead role in the cult favorite, "The Falls: Testament of Love".Hannah recently moved to LA on her birthday of 2015 and since then has worked steadily in TV and film, with her 2016 credits including Amazon''s "Good Girls Revolt", CBS''s "NCIS", "The Young & The Restless", and "CSI: Cyber", and TNT''s "The Librarians". She will appear as the lead role in the upcoming feature, "Derailed", produced through MarVista Entertainment. Hannah continues to write and produce her own work as well.Hannah believes that gratitude and persistence win the day. Every time.::Hannah Barefoot', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Hannah Barefoot');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1416531', 'Chase Offerle is an actor, known for Thumbsucker (2005), Tracktown (2016) and T Is for Trichomoniasis (2011).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Chase Offerle');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5897836', 'Brent Kublick is an American actor born in Portland, Oregon. His love for movies and music started early on, watching Westerns with his dad, John and listening to music with his mom, Donna Lynn. Brent started playing the drums on cardboard boxes in his mom''s garage as a young kid. He got his first real drum set from a pawn shop at age 15 for $110.00 and started teaching himself to play. He always had dreams of going to Hollywood to take a shot in the entertainment business...Brent married his high school sweetheart, Michelle and started his own construction business, all the while playing the drums or bass guitar and vocals in local rock n roll bands around the Portland area. Fast forward several years and Brent had a very successful marriage, a successful construction career and had played in many unsuccessful local bands. After getting laid off for the first time in years, he went to a casting call for a television show they were filming in Portland, OR. He got the part and a few weeks later he was shooting scenes with Academy Award winner Timothy Hutton for the TNT hit show ''Leverage'' (The Experimental Job and The Corkscrew Job). It was then that the acting bug took hold. Brent started taking acting classes with Ted Rooney at Blanche-Rooney Studios and landed several small parts on other shows that were filming in the Portland area, i.e., ''Grimm'', ''Portlandia'' and ''The Librarians''. He also landed parts in several movies shooting in town, such as ''Gone'' starring Amanda Seyfried, ''All The Wilderness'' with Danny DeVito and ''South of Heaven'' with Daniel Baldwin.It was around this time that Brent got laid off for the third time in 4 years from his construction job and decided to start pursuing acting more seriously. He landed the part of Drunk Guy #1 in a bar scene in the movie ''Wild'' with Academy Award winner Reese Witherspoon. He then landed his first co-starring role in the independent film, Crimson and Clover.In the summer of 2015, he finally got the call from Hollywood to come act in his first starring role in a film shooting just outside the Hollywood Hills. This was the role of Bucefilus Quaid in the upcoming feature film,''Cold Sun''. This film had a test screening at the Cannes Film Festival in spring 2016 and is slated for release in 2017. Not long after, Brent got another call from Hollywood to play the lead role in the independent spaghetti-style western, ''Cold Chains, Hard Hearts & Bloody Hands''. This was an off-the-grid shoot with Brent doing all his own stunts (as he did in ''Cold Sun''). This movie premiered in Beverly Hills in 2016 to great reviews and has attracted national and international attention.Brent is committed to two more pictures in 2017 and looking forward to another year of making movies. Until then, stay tuned and check IMDB for updates. As Brent would say, "Peace, Love & Hollywood".::Michelle K', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Brent Kublick');
