INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('1967566', 'Italian model and actress born in Chieti on November 14 1980 she left her hometown when she was 17 to attend "Ribalte" Acting School in Rome featuring Maestro Enzo Garinei. Some years later got a State scholarship to attend the course "Acting for Screen". She worked as a model for advertising campaigns, fashion shows and photo shooting, working at the same time as actress in different stage such as TV shows and theatre plays. Her first role in a movie was in Giuseppe Tornatore''s The Unknown Woman (2006) where she played the Adacher''s secretary while also acting as the leading actress'' double for the nude-shots. In late 2006 she co-starred in the independent film "Le ferie di Licu" directed by Vittorio Moroni and some roles in Italian tv series such as I Cesaroni (2006), "Io non dimentico" and "Sotto casa". In 2007 she worked with Samuel MacFadden in the full length "Al termine della notte" which got her first prize as best actress in "Fata Morgana film festival". She also appeared in many TV Ads, Toyota and Fox Life, just to name some. She starred in the movie Amore 14 (2009) directed by Federico Moccia and early 2010 we saw her in one of the chapters of the new TV series "Crimini" called Cane Nero directed by Claudio Bonivento.She can speak Spanish, French, English, and Italian.::OrsonWelles1981', NULL, NULL, '1980-11-14', NULL, 'Giulia Di Quilio');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2382107', 'Giorgia Ferrero is an actress, known for The Great Beauty (2013), Quale amore (2006) and Amore che vieni, amore che vai (2008).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Giorgia Ferrero');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('5336300', 'Actress, author and pianist Melania Fiore honors degree in Performing Arts and Sciences at the University Roma 3 in 2006 and graduated with honors from the biennial drama school "Moliere" by Mario Scaccia in 2002, with a essay on "Galantuomo per Tradizione" by Giovanni Giraud, in which she plays the role of Elisa and "Shakespeare", installation of various scenes from the Bard''s works, in which he plays the role of Rosalinda''s "As You Like It." After graduating she performs in many Scaccia''s plays, including "Chicchignola" by Ettore Petrolini, "Alcyone" by Gabriele D''Annunzio, along with Stars of the Opera, "Teatro Comico e no" with texts by M. L. Spaziani, "L''Amore in Guerra", in its first edition, with lyrics by Bertolt Brecht and Salvatore Quasimodo.She worked in many companies while continuing to attends in many laboratories and play the piano, which he studied for over ten years under the guidance of Maestro Lamberto Desires. Share stories and began writing for the theater in 2008."La Terrazza" is selected for the Award Attilio Corsini and is staged at the Teatro Stabile Vittoria in Rome, "Il Testamento del Marchese del Grillo" with Enzo Garinei, where he is also an actress debuted at Ostia Antica and then on tour in Italy; "Ti richiamo fra dieci minuti" is signaled by the jury for the interpretation of the Italian Drama Festival 2009, at the Festival received the Special Jury Prize in 2010 with "L''Atto Unico della Felicità", which won the prize "Artist of the years" at the Festival Theatre of Calcata 2011. "L''Amore in Guerra" in its second edition, written by and starring Melania Fiore, dedicated to Scaccia, has been successfully replicated in two seasons. "Tutto il mio amore" in 2011 won the award for "Best Actress" at the Festival of Italian Drama, and Prize for "Best Short Theatre" at the Teatro dell''Orologio in 2012.She then performed in many important theatre festivals trough Italy.In 2012 is the female protagonist of the play "Assolo contro la ''ndragheta" by Enrico Bernard, directed by Virginia Barrett at the Teatro dell''Orologio in Rome and then on tour in Italy, starting from the Teatro del Giglio in Lucca in 2013.In 2012 was chosen by Paolo Sorrentino for a role in his film The Great Beauty (2013).::A.C.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Melania Fiore');
INSERT INTO imdb.person VALUES ('2308815', 'He is an imposing Italian actor with extensive filming experience.Over the years he played a wide range of characters from small quirky roles to lead in features. He was born in Bologna, but he grew up in Falcade, a small village in the Dolomites of Belluno. Since childhood, he had a great passion for acting, and in his early twenties, whilst at university, he started to attend acting classes and had his first professional experience in theatre and cinema. A few years later he decided move to Rome. He took part in several film and television productions and acted under the direction of great directors such as Paolo Sorrentino, Dario Argento, Claudio Cupellini, Giacomo Campiotti, Michele Placido and played opposite Jordi Molla, Moritz Bleibtreu, Elio Germano, Toni Servillo, Aziz Ansari, Francesco Salvi, Neri Marcorè, Filippo Timi, Gigi Proietti, Kim Rossi Stuart, Alessio Boni and Luca Barbareschi. His first leading role came when director Marco Luca Cattaneo cast him in the feature film Amore Liquido. The role earned him The Best Actor award at Milan International Film Festival (MIFF) and at Salento International Film Festival (SIFF).::Anonymous', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stefano Fregni');
