INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22952, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22953, 'This was inspired by Russian publicist and writer Yevgeny Petrov, who died in a plane crash serving as a war correspondent.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22955, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22957, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22958, 'Boaz Yakin previously directed the 2003 film, Uptown Girls, a film which also deals with a troubled adult bonding with an intelligent child.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22959, 'The scenes at the mayor''s mansion were filmed at the Bloomfield estate in Villanova, Pennsylvania. On April 4th (less than one month before the film''s release), the garage burst into flames, starting what would eventually become a four alarm fire that destroyed most of the third floor of the main house.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22960, 'Robert John Burke''s character in this movie is a corrupt NYPD Captain. In Law & Order: SVU his character works for Internal Affairs and investigates corrupt NYPD officials. In Person of Interest he plays a crooked member of the NYPD.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22961, 'Hank Amos and Jason Statham both starred in The Expendables 2010');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22962, 'Dekalb Ave subway station and Canal St station were filmed at Cortlandt St station.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22963, 'The getaway coming out of the subway is filmed on the corner of East Broadway and Rutger St., shooting from the southeastern side of the crossing.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22964, 'Lawrence Bender: The bartender who hands Jason Statham a fork.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23242, 'In an introduction from Edgar Wright, he revealed that there was little to no CGI or green screen used to film the car chase sequences. The driving is all practically done.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22966, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22967, 'The first fully Chinese-funded film to have a Hollywood star in the lead.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22974, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22998, 'A good deal of the shots in the film depicting "Harvard''s Campus" were in fact filmed at Johns Hopkins University in Baltimore, including the opening scene in the trailer for the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22976, 'During one of the depositions, it is mentioned that the invention of Facebook made Mark Zuckerberg "the biggest thing on a campus that included nineteen Nobel Laureates, fifteen Pulitzer Prize winners, two future Olympians, and a movie star." One of the lawyers then asks, "Who was the movie star?" and the response is, "Does it matter?" This movie star was, in fact, Natalie Portman, who was enrolled at Harvard from 1999 to 2003 and helped screenwriter Aaron Sorkin by providing him insider information about goings-on at Harvard at the time Facebook first appeared there.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22977, 'Mark Zuckerberg originally planned never to see this movie. He ended up taking several of his employees to see it. He later remarked that, despite some of the film''s inaccuracies, they got his clothing right.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22978, 'The only scene Jesse Eisenberg had a problem with was the scene where Mark Zuckerberg films his friends jumping into a swimming pool from a rooftop. Originally Zuckerberg, instead of just filming it, was supposed to join in as well. Eisenberg couldn''t imagine Zuckerberg having that kind of fun. By the time it came to film the scene he was relieved the script had been changed so he just observes it instead.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22979, 'When Mark is posting on his art final under an alias, he is using the alias Tyler Durden, a main character of Fight Club (1999), another David Fincher film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22980, 'Natalie Portman revealed during "Newsweek''s 2011 Oscar Roundtable" that she gave a dinner party for writer Aaron Sorkin, while he was writing the script for this movie, to which she invited a bunch of her friends from Harvard. She wanted to give him the chance to listen to first-hand stories about the social life at Harvard University.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22981, 'Jesse Eisenberg and Andrew Garfield became good friends during filming. According to Eisenberg, the dramatic rivalry between their characters was hard for the two because it affected them emotionally.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22982, 'Justin Timberlake was the only actor who met his real-life character (Sean Parker) before the founding of Facebook and this film. Armie Hammer and Josh Pence met their real-life characters, the Winklevoss twins after filming. The twins enjoyed Hammer and Pence''s performance so much they attended a couple screenings of the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22983, 'Bill Gates is portrayed by Steve Sires, a "professional Gates impersonator," but his voice was dubbed by a "24-year-old African American kid with dreadlocks," who just happened to sound like Gates.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22984, 'Andrew Garfield came into rehearsal with a copy of Economics for Dummies. Inspired by that move, Jesse Eisenberg bought C++ for Dummies. According to Eisenberg, both he and Garfield read the introductions of their books and then put them down.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22985, 'David Fincher''s favorite line in the film is, "I''m just checking your math on that. Yes, I got the same thing."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22986, 'The Winklevoss twins were both played by actor Armie Hammer. However, Ralph Lauren model Josh Pence played one of them strictly from the neck down. His face was digitally replaced with Hammer''s to make them appear identical, as the two men are unrelated and look nothing alike. The two spent 10 months in twin boot camp to match one another''s subtle movements and rapport.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22987, 'As part of his research, Jesse Eisenberg read a copy of Mark Zuckerberg''s college application. Zuckerberg''s essay focused on his love of fencing, so Eisenberg took a couple of lessons. He quickly realized it affected his posture and the way he moved, and applied that knowledge to his portrayal of the character.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22988, 'Armie Hammer was forced to eat a lot of junk food to keep his weight up. All of the rowing he had to do for the film would have made him lose too much weight otherwise.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22989, 'The real Lawrence H. Summers called the film''s portrayal of his meeting with the Winkelvoss twins "fairly accurate". He went on to say "I''ve heard it said that I can be arrogant. If that''s true, I surely was on that occasion. One of the things you learn as a college president is that if an undergraduate is wearing a tie and jacket on Thursday afternoon at three o''clock, there are two possibilities. One is that they''re looking for a job and have an interview; the other is that they are an asshole. This was the latter case. Rarely, have I encountered such swagger, and I tried to respond in kind."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22990, 'The real Mark Zuckerberg had never heard of an Appletini before he had seen the film. After he tried one, he liked it so much he made the Appletini Facebook''s official drink.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22991, 'Andrew Garfield was originally asked to audition for Mark Zuckerberg but David Fincher decided he was too good at wearing his heart on his sleeve to play such an emotionally guarded character. Garfield found it helpful to go from reading for Mark to reading for Eduardo, because he felt that Eduardo tried to understand Mark through Mark''s point of view.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22992, 'Shortly after receiving an Academy Award nomination for his performance, Saturday Night Live hosted Jesse Eisenberg and Nicki Minaj. During his opening monologue, he was interrupted by the real Mark Zuckerberg.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22993, 'Aaron Sorkin directed the last shot in the film. David Fincher announced he was leaving- Sorkin thought it was a joke until the production crew came up to him asking how to film it. It only amounted to a second''s worth of footage anyway, but Sorkin got to announce the final wrap at the end.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22994, 'Josh Pence was on a Rowing Team in his college years and even rowed against the Winklevoss twins.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22995, 'After casting, David Fincher forbade principal actors from meeting their real-life counterparts until filming was completed.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22996, 'On the DVD commentary, Armie Hammer and Josh Pence recount meeting the real Divya Narendra and taking him to meet Max Minghella, who plays him in the film. As a practical joke, Hammer and Pence told Narendra to talk in an Indian accent, as Minghella had been worried about his portrayal and wanted it to be as accurate as possible. Narendra played along, much to the horror of Minghella. Hammer recalls, "Max just turns white and he just starts going, ''I''m so sorry! I''m so sorry! I''m so sorry!'' And profusely apologized to him, for, like, thirty minutes."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23304, 'The song "Easy" by The Commodores was requested for the movie by Ansel Elgort after Edgar Wright asked him if there were any songs he knew by heart.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23022, 'At one point, Mark calls the Winklevoss brothers the "Winklevi", facetiously using the Latin plural for nouns ending with an s. In fact, Mark Zuckerberg is quite the Latin scholar, having excelled in the classics while attending the Phillips Exeter Academy and taking advanced courses in subjects such as Greek and Latin while at Harvard.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23433, 'A clip from Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb (1964) shows on one television. It was one of Elvis Presley''s favorite movies.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22997, 'Some behind-the-scenes footage presented as a DVD extra reveals that during the filming of the "facemash montage" (which shows various groups of Harvard students perusing facemash and rating Harvard women against each other for relative attractiveness), one of the actors was instructed to say, "of course she''s hot; she''s Natalie Portman" while comparing two female Harvard students. That dialogue didn''t make it into the finished film, but another oblique reference to Portman''s presence on campus did (she is the movie star referred to during the deposition).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (22999, 'During the night club scene the extras are miming their dancing and the music was added in post-production. Jesse Eisenberg and Justin Timberlake had to shout their lines as though they were talking over the music. Eisenberg said it was a challenge to not lose their voices.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23000, 'Most outfits that Mark wears in the film are things that the real Mark Zuckerberg has been seen wearing in pictures, with at least one exception, a T-shirt from a theatre company that Jesse Eisenberg had belonged to.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23001, 'In October 2010, the real Sean Parker told Vanity Fair that he actually once met Justin Timberlake and that Timberlake wanted to get to know him better for his preparation for his role in this movie. Parker then replied getting to know the real Sean Parker wouldn''t help Timberlake at all, because the Parker from Aaron Sorkin''s script has little to do with the real person.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23002, 'When Facebook hits one million members, the number 1,000,046 appears on the screen after Sean Parker requests a refresh. The producers purposely chose the number to correspond with the running time of the movie at 1:46:46.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23003, 'According to David Fincher, Harvard wasn''t very helpful to the crew when they wanted to get as realistic a portrayal as possible of campus life. They had refused filming there ever since significant physical damage to the campus during the shooting of Love Story (1970). Other schools had to fill in for it instead.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23004, 'Rashida Jones who plays an associate of Mark Zuckerberg''s attorney was a graduate of Harvard University, the school Zuckerberg attended.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23005, 'Before filming, Jesse Eisenberg created a false Facebook account for research. Eisenberg opened his account under the name of Peter Sagal, the host of the radio show Wait, Wait... Don''t Tell Me! (2008), which Eisenberg was listening to at the time. He closed the account when filming wrapped.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23006, 'The original banner at the top of Facebook.com included a stylized portrait of a young Al Pacino. It was designed by Andrew McCollum, a friend of Mark Zuckerberg. The banner used on the website in the film uses a portrait of actor Jesse Eisenberg (who plays Zuckerberg).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23007, 'Because director David Fincher was unable to find any suitable identical twin actors to play real-life identical twins Cameron Winklevoss and Tyler Winklevoss, two unrelated actors were hired to play each brother - Armie Hammer as Cameron and Josh Pence as Tyler. Fincher thought that Hammer looked more like the real brothers, so for some scenes, the visual effects team photographed Hammer speaking Tyler''s lines and created a computer-generated model of his face to paste over Pence''s. Traditional split-screen work, with Hammer''s separate performances as each brother stitched together in the same frame, was also used.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23008, 'The notepad that Mark carries in the deposition scenes was Jesse Eisenberg''s own idea, as part of his way of assessing his own performances after each take.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23009, 'Justin Timberlake lost 15-17 pounds for his role in this movie. He felt that making himself look skinnier would make him look younger.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23010, 'Amy''s line in French ("Tu fais l''amour à la jolie fille") roughly translates in English, "You''ve made love to a pretty girl."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23011, 'Armie Hammer studied Jeremy Irons'' performance in Dead Ringers (1988) to get an idea of how to play twin brothers.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23012, 'The song that plays during the Opening credits is only played two more times during the film, and each time, Trent Reznor recorded the piano from farther away. Giving the illusion of echoing and isolation in the final cut.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23013, 'The note "U dick" that Mark is handed by a girl in class is a replacement of a more profane word that the MPAA wouldn''t approve for a PG-13 rating.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23014, 'After Mark finishes the coding marathon in his dorm room, he then closes his eyes and slowly moves his head back and forth, and Eduardo asks him, "Mark, are you praying?" On the DVD commentary, Aaron Sorkin explained that what Mark was doing was davening, a word that comes from Yiddish and which generally refers to prayer in Judaism, but which also specifically refers to the type of head and body movements that Jews traditionally make while praying. Sorkin mentioned on the commentary that he considered writing Eduardo''s line as "Mark, are you davening?" instead of "Mark, are you praying?" to make it clearer to the audience what Mark was doing.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23015, 'Eduardo Saverin was the one who brought this story to Ben Mezrich''s attention in the first place, but has since refused to speak with him.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23016, 'The line about Cameron Winklevoss and Tyler Winklevoss going after Mark Zuckerberg like the Cobra Kai kids going after Ralph Macchio in The Karate Kid (1984) was something they''d said to Ben Mezrich during his research interviews for the book.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23017, 'During the climactic confrontation between Zuckerberg and Saverin, Zuckerberg can be seen wearing an Arm & Hammer t-shirt. Armie Hammer, who plays the Winklevoss twins, is named after his great grandfather Armand Hammer, who is speculated to be named after the company.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23018, 'There is actually a Facebook page for "Erica Albright," a character in the film. The profile pictures are of the actress Rooney Mara who plays Albright. It is also listed that she attended Boston University.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23019, 'Despite the "Erica Albright" subplot and Mark''s depiction in this movie as being generally maladroit with women, during much of the period covered by the film, the real Mark Zuckerberg was actually dating fellow Harvard student Priscilla Chan. Chan, who was one of the very first people ever to join Facebook (on February 5, 2004), graduated from medical school in 2012, the same year that she and Zuckerberg got married. They had their first child, daughter Maxima Chan Zuckerberg, in 2015.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23020, 'In Zombieland (2009), Jesse Eisenberg''s character said that the best part of the zombie apocalypse was not having to worry about updating his Facebook status. While making that film, he had to have the directors and cast explain to him what a Facebook status was.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23305, 'Wright was insistent on filming most of the chase scenes in the daylight because it created an "extra air of collision tension."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23021, 'Aaron Sorkin and David Fincher wanted to do the movie based solely on a 14-page book proposal that somehow got leaked to Gawker.com right about the time 21 (2008) came out; the book hadn''t even been written yet, and Ben Mezrich wound up writing it in a hotel room with Sorkin right next to him, handing Sorkin the chapters as they were finished.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23468, 'Jason Bateman and Jennifer Aniston appeared in The Switch (2010).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23052, 'The Thirsty Scholar Somerville Bar and Grill featured at the start of the film is very close to Harvard University. However, it is expensive and unlikely to be frequented by students (a burger is $12).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23053, 'On his director commentary David Fincher tells people with complaints to send Aaron Sorkin an email and proceeds to name it (though it is bleeped out by the sound editor).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23054, 'David Fincher and Armie Hammer share a birthday (August 28th)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23055, 'Trent Reznor & Atticus Ross also produced the music scores for "The Girl With The Dragon Tattoo"(2011), which also starred Rooney Mara.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23318, 'Edgar Wright directly reached out to hip hop artists Big Boi and Killer Mike for cameo appearances in the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23023, 'Facebook co-founder Dustin Moskovitz called the film a "dramatization of history ... it is interesting to see my past rewritten in a way that emphasizes things that didn''t matter, (like the Winklevosses, who I''ve still never even met and had no part in the work we did to create the site over the past 6 years) and leaves out things that really did (like the many other people in our lives at the time, who supported us in innumerable ways)". According to Moskovitz: "A lot of exciting things happened in 2004, but mostly we just worked a lot and stressed out about things; the version in the trailer seems a lot more exciting, so I''m just going to choose to remember that we drank ourselves silly and had a lot of sex with coeds.... The plot of the book/script unabashedly attacked [Zuckerberg], but I actually felt like a lot of his positive qualities come out truthfully in the trailer (soundtrack aside). At the end of the day, they cannot help but portray him as the driven, forward-thinking genius that he is".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23024, 'Aziz Ansari auditioned for the role of Divya Narendra. In a New York Times article written by Ansari, he admitted that his audition was "horrible" but he did not like that a non-Indian actor was cast.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23025, 'Joseph Mazzello claimed that he accepted the role as Dustin Moskovitz partly because he had just completed a World War II miniseries, The Pacific (2010), and playing a college student sounded like fun after such an exhausting role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23026, 'Reported to be R-rated during production, but was edited down to PG-13 to make it accessible for a wider audience.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23027, 'Aaron Sorkin''s small role as the ad executive was not his own idea; David Fincher was reportedly very insistent that he do it.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23028, 'Facebook CEO Mark Zuckerberg was not involved with this film adaptation of author Ben Mezrich''s biographical novel ''The Accidental Billionaires'', neither did he meet Jesse Eisenberg prior to, or during, the movie shoot.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23029, 'The song that plays in the car during the scene where mark goes to the meeting in his pajamas is a song by *NSYNC, whose lead singer Justin Timberlake plays Sean Parker in the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23030, 'Shia LaBeouf turned down the role of Mark.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23031, 'Total footage shot: 268 hours / 35060 GB digital data at 4K resolution fit into 2192 16GB SD cards / 1.45 million feet (35 mm film) equivalent');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23032, 'As an indicator of David Fincher''s habit of shooting multiple takes, Armie Hammer pointed to a shot in which he takes exactly one bite of a hamburger before the scene ends, claiming that he was gorged by the time they wrapped shooting that scene.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23033, 'Main video editing was done with Final Cut Pro, with extensive work on tweaking, conforming and fixing up shots done with Adobe software, namely After Effects and Premiere. In 2011, the film became the first Academy Award-winner for Best Editing that utilized Final Cut Pro.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23034, 'Divya Narendra said that he was "initially surprised" to see himself portrayed by the non-Indian actor Max Minghella, but also admitted that the actor did a "good job in pushing the dialogue forward and creating a sense of urgency in what was a very frustrating period."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23035, 'Despite the fact that director David Fincher has been a big proponent of digital filmmaking since Zodiac (2007), this is his first film to have been completely shot digitally (both Zodiac and The Curious Case of Benjamin Button (2008) had certain shots/segments shot on film).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23036, 'While Mark forgets to pick up Eduardo at the airport in the film, Mark Zuckerberg actually remembered to pick up Eduardo Saverin in real life. It was changed in the movie to add more depth to the characters.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23037, 'At the time of release, there were about 750 million active users on Facebook. If everyone who had a Facebook account at the time went to go see the movie during its theatrical release, it would have grossed somewhere around US $6 billion.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23038, 'Steven Soderbergh owned two of the four Red One cameras used in the movie''s production, which he lent to the crew. He is given special thanks in the end credits.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23039, 'Mark Zuckerberg thought the movie was "interesting" as he said when he met Jesse Eisenberg, who portrayed him in the picture, on Saturday Night Live: Jesse Eisenberg/Nicki Minaj (2011), when Eisenberg was hosting.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23040, 'This is the second Ben Mezrich adaptation that is produced by Kevin Spacey''s production company, Trigger Street. The first one was "Bringing Down the House," which became 21 (2008).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23041, 'There is only one hand-held shot in the entire film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23042, 'At the D8 conference hosted by D: All Things Digital on June 2, 2010, host Kara Swisher told Mark Zuckerberg she knew he was not happy with the film being based on him, to which he replied, "I just wished that nobody made a movie of me while I was still alive." Zuckerberg stated to Oprah Winfrey that the drama and partying of the film is mostly fiction, explaining "this is my life, so I know it''s not so dramatic," and that he spent most of the past six years focusing, working hard, and coding Facebook. Speaking to an audience at Stanford University, Zuckerberg stated that the film portrayed his motivations for creating Facebook inaccurately; instead of an effort to "get girls", he says he created the site because he enjoys "building things".[42] However, he added that the film accurately depicted his real-life wardrobe, saying, "It''s interesting the stuff that they focused on getting right - like every single shirt and fleece they had in that movie is actually a shirt or fleece that I own."[42]');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23043, 'The screenplay for this film was featured in the 2009 Blacklist; a list of the "most liked" unmade scripts of the year.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23044, 'There is a chapter in Ben Mezrich''s "The Accidental Billionaires" called "Cambridge, 1." which refers to an actual restaurant in Harvard Square where Mark Zukerberg held some of his initial meetings.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23306, 'In reference to the character of Doc, director Edgar Wright described him as "like one of those awful father figures who can be great in rare moments."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23045, 'The sequence where Mark leaves a classroom and meets the Winklevii in the hallway was filmed at the University of Southern California in Los Angeles. The classroom he exits is in a different building (Taper Hall of Humanities) from the hallway in which he meets the twins (Grace Ford Salvatori Hall).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23046, 'Included among the "1001 Movies You Must See Before You Die", edited by Steven Schneider.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23047, 'Rooney Mara teamed with director David Fincher again in The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo (2011).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23048, 'The film cast includes one Oscar winner: Aaron Sorkin; and four Oscar nominees: Jesse Eisenberg, Andrew Garfield, Rooney Mara and Justin Timberlake.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23049, 'Alfred Molina was considered for the role of Lawrence H. Summers before Douglas Urbanski got the part.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23050, 'Cameo: Josh Pence: The man that Mark and Eduardo send away from the restroom in the night club by remarking, "Sorry man, a couple of girls are freshening up in there," is Josh Pence, who plays Tyler Winklevoss from the neck down.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23051, 'In the opening sequence, when Mark opens his laptop, you will notice a ''K''-gear icon at the lower-left corner of the screen. That icon is what KDE uses for its version of the Start Menu (known sometimes as the K-menu)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23056, 'The cocaine scene had to be very carefully edited to avoid an R-rating, due to the depiction of sexualized drug use. No shot could show the girl''s body and the insufflator in the same frame.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23057, 'As Kevin Spacey is executive producer, both the latter and Jesse Eisenberg had portrayed Superman''s archenemy Lex Luther in Superman Returns and Batman v. Superman: Dawn of Justice respectively.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23058, 'When Mark types the word ''facebook'' in a blog post during the FaceMash scene, beneath the word appears a collection of dots indicating an unrecognised word on the blogging software.  The word ''Facebook'' is now an acceptable and globally known term on almost all pieces of software such as Microsoft Word and Google.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23059, 'Jonathan Groff auditioned for the role of Sean Parker.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23060, 'Aaron Sorkin: The ad executive that Zuckerberg and Saverin meet in New York is played (in a credited appearance) by Sorkin, the screenwriter for this film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23061, 'The opening breakup scene with Jesse Eisenberg and Rooney Mara ran eight script pages and took 99 takes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23063, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23064, 'The characters played by Michael Rosenbaum and Kevin Spacey battle at one point; both men have portrayed the DC Comics character Lex Luthor.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23218, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23219, 'On November 3, 2017, while the film was in post-production, Netflix canceled the project in light of multiple sexual assault and harassment allegations made against Kevin Spacey.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23221, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23222, 'When the project was in development Angelina Jolie was offered the lead female role of Gail Harris, the mother of John Paul Getty III, but declined. When the project was officially announced, Natalie Portman had been offered the Gail Harris role. However, she had to decline as she was giving birth to her second baby. Michelle Williams was finally cast.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23223, 'Director Ridley Scott worked with actor Balthazar Getty, who is the son of John Paul Getty III, on White Squall (1996). With All the Money in the World (2017) Scott is now telling the story of Balthazar Getty''s father, who was kidnapped in Italy in 1973.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23224, 'Originally, Jack Nicholson was offered the role of Jean Paul Getty. but he declined the offer. Kevin Spacey eventually signed on for the role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23225, 'Filming started on Mark Wahlberg''s birthday, June 5th.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23226, 'Alongside Alien: Covenant (2017), this film marks the second time Ridley Scott has directed two films released in a single year. The first time was in 2001, when Scott films Hannibal (2001) and Black Hawk Down (2001) were released.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23228, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23229, 'Judd Nelson was in the TV movie with the same title. He''s now playing the father role of his previous character.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23230, 'Emma Roberts was originally to join in the fifth season of American Horror Story (2011), but she had to leave to shoot this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23231, 'Ansel Elgort and Kevin Spacey also starred in Baby Driver (2017).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23232, 'Second collaboration between actresses Billie Lourd and Emma Roberts both appeared in Fox''s TV hit Scream Queens (2015) as Chanel Oberin and Chanel #3');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23233, 'Ansel Elgort and Suki Waterhouse also starred in Insurgent (2015).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23234, 'Billie Lourd, Emma Roberts, and Deneen Tyler all starred in Scream Queens');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23235, 'Ansel Elgort and Taron Egerton were both in the running for the role of young Han Solo in Solo: A Star Wars Story (2018).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23236, 'Both Cary Elwes and Bokeem Woodbine were on Life in Pieces (2015).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23237, 'Ansel Elgort is playing Joe hunt. Fellow co-star Judd Nelson played Joe hunt in the 1987 version of this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23238, 'This is Ansel Egort and Kevin Spacey''s second collaboration. The first is Baby Driver (2017)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23240, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23241, 'Jamie Foxx would often stay and watch Kevin Spacey''s scenes, even when he wasn''t in the scene. Jamie Foxx says it''s nice to have the opportunity to watch great artists performing their roles. He claims he watches a lot of foreign movies and independent movies as well, and said he''d love to watch Gustavo Goulart performing a theater play or even a music concert in USA, as Jamie Foxx considers Gustavo Goulart "an amazingly talented kid who became a breathtaking adult actor" (Foxx''s own words).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23243, 'The character Joseph was originally written to be much older, around the mid-80s. CJ Jones (who plays Joseph, a deaf character) was discovered and recommended by casting director Francine Maisler. Jones is deaf in real life; Ansel Elgort had to learn sign language to communicate with him.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23244, 'The tracking shot in the beginning of the movie where Baby gets coffee took 28 takes. The 21st take is the one used in the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23245, 'Jon Hamm''s role was written for him, and he is the only actor from the first table read to end up in the final film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23246, 'The extensive collection of sunglasses and iPods that Baby owns were not bought by him; they were taken from cars he stole. In an interview, Edgar Wright said: ''If he has been stealing cars since he was 12, the main thing he would have inherited from these stolen cars are people''s sunglasses and iPods.''');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23247, 'Whenever Edgar Wright had Jamie Foxx and Kevin Spacey in the same shot, he would whisper to a colleague: "Double Oscar shot!"');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23248, 'On the first day of filming, Jamie Foxx watched Jon Hamm on the monitor and uttered to himself "he handsome."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23319, 'Costume designer Courtney Hoffman had Ansel Elgort try on 80 different jackets before settling on a look for Baby.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23321, 'The Mercedes-Benz S550 driven by Doc was supplied by Mercedes-Benz; all of them used were destroyed and scrapped by the time filming wrapped.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23249, 'Edgar Wright had been sitting on this idea for a film for many years. His first use of it was a music video he directed for British electronic duo Mint Royale and their track "Blue Song". The video stars Noel Fielding as a music-loving getaway driver for a group of bank robbers, one of whom is Wright''s regular Nick Frost. A clip from the video is featured in the film when channels are being flipped through on the television in Baby''s apartment.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23250, 'In almost every scene where no music is playing, you can hear a slight ringing in the background (the sound of Baby''s tinnitus).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23251, 'Emma Stone was originally sought to play Debora, but dropped out to make La La Land (2016).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23252, 'When Edgar Wright wanted Ansel Elgort to be more stern in a shot, he used the code words "Man Driver!" He taught him the "Kubrick look" by showing Ansel a picture on his phone of Malcolm McDowell in character in A Clockwork Orange (1971).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23253, 'When Baby is flipping through the channels near the beginning of the film, several lines of dialogue from different movies can be heard ("you are so beautiful," "they grow up so freaking fast," "how''s that working out for you?" and "we''re partners. There''s nothing that matters to me more than our friendship"). Each one of these lines appears later in the film as a line of dialogue.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23254, 'The first R-rated movie to be given permission to show footage from a Disney film (Monsters, Inc. (2001)). Pete Docter, the director of "Monsters, Inc.", is given a ''special thanks'' credit as a result.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23255, 'Barbra Streisand''s experience with tinnitus was the basis for a scene in the movie where Jamie Foxx''s character is required to say, "Do I look like I know a f*cking thing about Barbra f*cking Streisand?" Knowing Barbra is close friends with Jamie in real life (who knew?), Edgar was worried about how she would react. Jamie''s response to Edgar''s worries was "Barbra''s gangsta." In 2016 Jamie Foxx sang a duet with Streisand on her ENCORE album.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23256, 'According to Edgar Wright, each script sent to the main actors that are wanted for their respective roles includes an Ipod that contains list of songs that is to be played (arranged in specific order) while reading a particular scene for the movie in order to emphasize the tone.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23257, 'Most, if not all of the gun shots in the film are in time with beat of the music.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23258, 'During the opening credits, when Baby is going to get coffee and listening to "Harlem Shuffle," lyrics to the song can be seen on graffiti, signs, and posters as he passes them.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23259, 'Worried he would lose communications link with his actors or cameras, Edgar Wright had himself strapped to the shooting car, rather than being in a follow car. Jon Hamm joked that he had to perform while looking at a "sunburnt muppet" flopping about - referring to Edgar.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23260, 'This film is named after Simon & Garfunkel''s song "Baby Driver" from their 1970 album "Bridge Over Troubled Water." The song appears in the film during the end credits.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23261, 'First Edgar Wright film to be shot in the United States.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23262, 'Edgar Wright started to work on this film in 1995, but didn''t finish the script until 2011, and the film until 2017. However, he received the advance for it in 2007. He introduced the world premiere of the film at SXSW by thanking his producer for not suing him for this.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23263, 'A song is played in the background of nearly every scene in the film. Also, whenever a song plays in 4/4 rhythm, a shot almost always cuts in one of the four beats.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23264, 'Originally set in LA, the film was finally shot in Atlanta. Other cities with tax incentives were ruled out as being too cold or fell through at the last minute. Wright had local writers and location scouts help him rewrite the film to make it authentically Atlanta.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23265, 'In the restaurant scene, Kevin Spacey''s character is seen talking to Big Boi (of Outkast) and Killer Mike (of Run the Jewels). They also contribute a song to the film''s soundtrack.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23266, 'There are multiple references to the "Back to the Future Trilogy" with Kevin Spacey''s character named "Doc" (Back to the Future) and Jon Bernthal''s character is named "Griff" (Back to the Future Part II). The actor "Flea" who played the character "Needles" in Back to the Future Parts II & III plays a small role in this film as "Eddie." The character "Doc" in the film also mentions a past job called "The Spirit of ''85," which is the year the first Back to the Future was released (1985).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23267, 'Edgar Wright timed the character''s movements to the beat of the film''s songs.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23268, 'When Doc plans the heist for Bats, Eddie, and JD, his dialogue can''t be heard over Baby''s music. The dialogue is present in the trailer, however, because Edgar Wright thought it deserved to be heard in that context.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23269, 'The opening credits use a one take shot of Baby walking to buy coffee and then walking back, reminiscent of the famous opening of Shaun of the Dead (2004), where Shaun walks to the shop and then back home in one shot (which is later repeated once the zombie outbreak has begun).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23270, 'In a recent interview with THR ( The Hollywood Reporter) Edgar Wright explains why Baby (Ansel Egort) doesn''t use smartphones for his music and calls. It''s because modern day technology like smartphones can be tracked, so by using burners and iPods, Baby can stay off the grid.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23271, 'In early 2017, director Edgar Wright tweeted Meryl Streep''s in our movie!'' After he quickly deleted it, many people speculated whether or not Streep was in the film. While she doesn''t appear in the film itself, Streep does appear on a TV screen while Baby is flipping through channels in a clip from It''s Complicated (2009).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23272, 'During promotion, Edgar Wright jokingly referred to the film as part of a Simon and Garfunkel Cinematic Universe along with Marc Webb''s The Only Living Boy in New York (2017). Both films are named after Simon and Garfunkel songs.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23273, 'Baby and Debora are frequently dressed in black and white. In an interview, Ansel Elgort said it was to contrast with the other characters and to give their love story a more timeless feel.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23274, 'During his interview on the Nerdist Podcast, Edgar Wright admitted to putting a bunch of Easter eggs in this film. He told Chris Hardwick one of the cars has a license plate that''s represents the release date of another one of his films.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23275, 'Michael Douglas was considered for the role of Doc. Edgar Wright was responsible for his casting as Hank Pym in Ant-Man (2015) before Wright left the project.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23276, 'In keeping with the musical theme of the film, singers and musicians make appearances throughout. In addition to the already-mentioned Big Boi and Killer Mike appearance, Flea of the Red Hot Chili Peppers and Academy Award-winning songwriter Paul Williams appear in small roles. Jamie Foxx plays a major role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23277, 'During the casting process, the actors were sent a playlist of songs and were asked to play the music while reading the script.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23320, 'Doc''s car, the Mercedes Benz S550, had to have its computer systems modified for the chase scenes since the car is engineered to correct itself when it goes out of control.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23278, 'The Mike Myers masks actually were supposed to be the masks of Michael Myers from the Halloween series but the producers were unable to obtain legal permission. Edgar Wright then reached out to the comedian Mike Myers about using masks of his likeness instead, who thought the scene was funny and gave his blessing.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23279, 'DIRECTOR CAMEO: Edgar Wright is seen reflected in the music shop window during the first coffee run. Wright said on Twitter he was following the shot and planned to remove the reflection in post, but decided to leave it in.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23280, 'The car Baby drives in the opening scene is a 2006 Subaru WRX in San Remo Red.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23281, 'Blues rock singer Jon Spencer, whose song "Bellbottoms" is used in the first robbery, plays a jail guard.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23282, 'This is the first time since A Fistful of Fingers (1995) that Edgar Wright is the sole credited writer on one of his films.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23283, 'As this movie is filmed in Atlanta and Edgar Wright added many touches to make it authentically Atlantan, when the Bo''s Diner chef answers the phone and says "what''ll ya have?," this is most likely a reference to the famous Atlanta diner The Varsity, where the employees take your order by asking "what''ll ya have?"');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23284, 'When Edgar Wright began writing the script, he only had ten songs to start with. The final film had thirty, according to the published playlist. The song Smokey Joe''s La La was a very late replacement for the B. Bumble and the Stingers'' Nut Rocker during post-production as after several test screenings Wright felt that "it started to get on his tits" that he re-shot part of that scene. Also, Easy by The Commodores was included after Ansel Elgort was cast as Wright found out during audition that it was one of the songs that Elgort knows very well and could sing / lip sync. That moment won him the title role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23285, 'Ansel Elgort beat Logan Lerman and John Boyega for the title role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23286, 'Partially filmed in Juliette, Georgia, the same area that Fried Green Tomatoes (1991) was filmed. The Whistle Stop Cafe is still in business there.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23287, 'Bats names three titles that are considered "hex songs:" The Guns N'' Roses cover of "Knockin'' on Heaven''s Door," The Eagles'' "Hotel California," and Boyz II Men''s "End of the Road." "Knockin''" was based on a superstition held by an ex-convict that Edgar Wright interviewed, where he said that a robbery gig would be called off if the song is played over the radio prior to executing the plan. "Hotel California" is one of the songs that in real-life Jamie Foxx absolutely detests (he ad-libbed that line). While there has yet to be an explanation for End of the Road, it highlights the complicated relationship between Baby and Debora throughout the film that he was forced to drop things for Doc''s heists.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23288, 'Chloë Grace Moretz was once attached to this project. She later dropped out of this film and The Little Mermaid (2017), among others.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23289, 'One of the red Subaru WRX used in the film was given to Ansel Elgort for his birthday after he pleaded with the filmmakers to give him the car after filming had wrapped up.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23290, 'The car seen at the start of the film (Red 2007 Subaru Impreza) is the same model of car seen at the ending of Edgar Wright''s 2007 film Hot Fuzz.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23291, 'During the second robbery, the characters wear Austin Powers masks from Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery (1997). The song that plays during this sequence, "Neat Neat Neat" by The Damned, features the lyrics ''be a man, kinda a mystery man.''');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23292, 'The electronic "beep-boop" that accompanies the opening of the Post Office''s sliding doors to Baby and Samm (Doc''s nephew) as they enter and leave is a sound effect used in Ridley Scott''s Blade Runner (1982), pitched up one octave.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23293, 'Jamie Foxx and Kevin Spacey are the fifth and sixth Academy Award winning celebrities featured in an Edgar Wright movie. Jim Broadbent, Cate Blanchett and Peter Jackson were in Hot Fuzz (2007). Brie Larson was in Scott Pilgrim vs. the World (2010).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23294, 'During one robbery, the group wear Austin Powers masks. Kevin Spacey played Dr. Evil in the movie-within-a-movie "Austinpussy" in Austin Powers in Goldmember (2002).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23295, 'The film cast includes three Oscar winners: Kevin Spacey, Jamie Foxx and Paul Williams.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23296, 'Discounting Basic Instinct (1992), which was produced by Carolco, and District 9 (2009), which was released while the Tri-Star brand was used part-time, this is Tri-Star Pictures'' highest-grossing production as a full-time studio since Hook (1991).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23297, 'Kevin Spacey and Ansel Elgort will also be in Billionaire Boys Club (2017).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23298, 'Ansel Elgort had been trained in ballet and other forms of dance since childhood, a skill which proved to be useful for the musically choreographed action scenes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23299, 'Edgar Wright got the idea for Doc to bring his "nephew" while scoping out a bank after interviewing a real ex-con who revealed that he did just that prior to a robbery.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23300, 'Director of Photography Bill Pope called the movie "a postmodern musical." Stating that "there''s not singing and dancing in the street but the world acts to music."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23301, 'Over 150 cars were used for the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23302, 'The studio pressured Edgar Wright to cut the foot chase scene because the movie was starting to go over-budget. Wright deferred a portion of his directing fee to ensure the scene was completed.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23303, 'Both Ansel Elgort and Jon Hamm received a month of driving training to prepare for the extensive and elaborate chase scenes in the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23307, 'The studio requested that the scene in which Baby mispronounces the band, T-Rex as "Trex" be cut from the film because it made the character sound dumb, though Edgar Wright refused.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23308, 'Edgar Wright generally doesn''t allow improv on his sets, though he did make a few exceptions this time, namely for Jamie Foxx.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23309, 'All of the driving scenes were accomplished without the aid of visual effects or CGI.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23310, 'One of the film''s technical consultants was Joe Loya, who served a seven year prison sentence for bank robbery in the early 90s.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23312, 'In a scene featuring Baby''s home audio rig, you can see an album cover of the Incredible Bongo Band''s record Bongo Rock. One of the songs on this album, Apache, became famous for being used for mixing by pioneering hip hop deejay Kool Herc in the seventies. In fact most people consider him one of the first people to mix and scratch records to create new songs. The Apache break-sample is still used today. Thus the album cover can be seen as a reference to the early pioneers of mixing, being the predecessors of Baby.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23323, 'Costume designer Courtney Hoffman suggested giving Lily James'' character, Deborah, beat up boots to show that "she''s not committed to this life of being a waitress and can take off anytime."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23324, 'During the action scenes of the final heist, two songs from Dutch bands are played. The first is Hocus Pocus by Focus, the second Radar Love by Golden Earring.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23325, 'During the opening credits, title sequence, and song, some of the graffiti in the background of the scene perfectly matches up with the song lyrics.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23326, 'Edgar Wright admitted to being a bit star-struck when working with Kevin Spacey.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23327, 'Despite Edgar Wright insisting on using less CGI, visual effects company Double Negative provided around 450 VFX shots, mostly for clean-up, digital cars, background objects and combining practical shots.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23328, 'For research purposes, Edgar Wright interviewed ex-convicts while writing the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23329, 'Brighton Rock by Queen was always intended to be used in the final chase scene.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23330, 'When star Ansel Elgort was given the script, it was given to him on an iPad with emojis that played music for their relevant scenes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23331, 'During the studio logos, you can hear a slight whine that resembles Baby''s tinnitus.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23332, 'The diner was the only set built for the movie, everything else was filmed on location.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23333, 'Ansel Elgort was in the shortlist of actors to play Han Solo in the upcoming Star Wars spin-off. In most scenes of this movie, he wears the black jacket with the white sleeves similar to Han Solo''s outfit.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23334, 'The role of Buddy was always intended for Jon Hamm.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23335, 'The collection of vinyl records in Joe''s apartment hints that he may have been passionate about music prior to losing his hearing.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23336, 'A few 2006 Subaru Impreza WRX was used in the film with varying modifications to the car. Some of them were a stock WRX STI that had its spoiler swapped for a conservative WRX versions and another featured modifications with over 320 horsepower, a heavier clutch, and differentials from an STI.One of the cars was an automatic with seat and controls fitted to the roof to enable the crew to film the actors "driving," without them having to worry about actually controlling the car. Another, a WRX with a modest power boost up to the high 200-horsepower range and converted to rear-wheel drive was considered by it''s stunt driver, Jeremy Fry, as his favorite to drive.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23337, 'The coffee run sequence was the first scene filmed for the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23338, 'A frequent issue the filmmakers encountered was finding copious amounts of leaves all over the streets of Atlanta. They often opted to shoot in urban settings in order to avoid them.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23339, 'According to Edgar Wright, many people thought that the diner set was a real restaurant and occasionally groups would enter and sit down to have lunch.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23340, 'Nearly all of the movie is shot on location in Atlanta, you can see in the opening walk that Doc''s office is inside the Healey Building, which is in Downtown. Oddly enough, the bank in the first heist (which is not a bank in real life), is in The Candler Building, which is less than three blocks away - not even a mile by car.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23341, 'Fellow director and friend of Edgar Wright, Robert Rodriguez, suggested Eiza Gonzales for the role of Darling.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23342, 'According to production designer Marcus Rowland, the 50s themed diner where Debora works was converted from an abandoned Denny''s.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23343, 'The character, Bats, gets annoyed when asked if he knew about Barbra Streisand, though in reality Jamie Foxx is close friends with her.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23344, 'Jamie Foxx was asked if Barbra Streisand would be offended by the joke made at her expense. Foxx, a friend of Babs, assured the team that she should would not, stating "Barbra''s gangsta."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23345, 'Multiple actors auditioned for the role of Baby''s foster father, Joseph, but CJ Jones was the only one who auditioned that was actually deaf.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23346, 'The chase scene following the second heist was partially shot on State Route 9 in Atlanta, also known as the Gladys Knight Highway.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23347, 'One of the cars, a 2006 Subaru Impreza WRX Limited, that was used as a stunt car had a number of modifications made for the film carried out by Allpro Subaru of Alpharetta. Georgia with further modifications for filming by Doug Wilkes at DBW Motorsport. This includes a conversion to rear wheel drive, upgraded rear differentials and a turbocharger from a 2004 WRX STIIt also was used in the music video for ''Chase Me" by Danger Mouse, Big Boi & Run The Jewels (containing scenes of the movie) by Subaru and Sony for its premiere in LA. It was auctioned off in August 2017 for $69,100 (enough for two brand new WRXs) via eBay despite it had "a few minor dings and scratches", had been resprayed from Crystal Gray Metallic racked up 168,000 miles on the odometer and been described as in a good condition.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23348, '15 Dodge Charger was supplied by Dodge in addition to a Challenger; by the time filming had wrapped, all but two were destroyed. 2 Chevrolet Blazers was used.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23349, 'Edgar Wright stated that the movie, The Driver (1978), was a major inspiration for Baby Driver.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23351, 'Three Oscar winners are featured in this movie, Kevin Spacey (who won two awards, Best Actor in a Supporting Role for The Usual Suspects and Best Actor in a Leading Role for American Beauty), Jamie Foxx (Best Actor in a Leading Role for Ray), and Paul Williams (Best Original Song for A Star is Born).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23352, 'During one scene where Baby is flicking through channels a short clip from Blue song by Mint Royale is shown. Edgar Wright directed this music video and has stated this is where he practiced the opening scene to Baby Driver.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23353, 'Jamie Foxx and Kevin Spacey were in both Horrible Bosses (2011) and Horrible Bosses 2 (2014).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23354, 'Edgar Wright was intent on using a song from The Damned in the soundtrack.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23355, 'Jamie Foxx''s line "That''s some Oscar shit right there." Was improvised');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23356, 'Baby''s first walk to get coffee (to "Harlem Shuffle") takes him out of the Healy Building on Forsyth St NW, around the first corner left into Poplar St NW, then to a coffee shop at the corner with Fairlie St NW. Several real landmarks can still be seen on Google Maps (such as Sidebar Bar), while other elements (such as the graffiti and the ATM) were obviously added by filmmakers.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23357, 'One of the red Subaru WRX used in the film was given to Ansel Elgort after he pleaded with the filmmakers to give him the car after filming had wrapped up.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23358, 'Edgar Wright began developing the story for Baby Driver shortly after wrapping production on his film, A Fistful of Fingers (1995).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23359, 'The film was originally set in Los Angeles, but was changed to Atlanta when the production moved to Georgia.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23360, 'Various crew members played extras during the action scenes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23512, 'Carla Gugino was attached for over a year to play Sarah Robertson, but had to withdraw last minute due to another project. Fortunately Demi Moore was able to join the project.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23361, 'Five 2006 Subaru Impreza WRX was used in the film had varying modifications to the car. Some of them were a stock WRX STI that had its spoiler swapped for a conservative WRX versions and another featured modifications with over 320 horsepower, a heavier clutch, and differentials from an STI.One of the cars was an automatic with seat and controls fitted to the roof to enable the crew to film the actors "driving," without them having to worry about actually controlling the car. Another, a WRX with a modest power boost up to the high 200-horsepower range and converted to rear-wheel drive was considered by its stunt driver, Jeremy Fry, as his favorite to drive.By the time filming wrapped up, three of them survived.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23362, 'Writer-director Edgar Wright conceived Baby Driver in 1994; he adapted the film''s original planned beginning into a 2003 music video he directed for Mint Royale''s "Blue Song," which starred Noel Fielding as a music-loving getaway driver for a group of bank robbers. A clip of the music video is shown briefly in the movie as the main character flips between television channels. Emma Stone and Michael Douglas were also being eyed to be in the cast. Wright enlisted Ryan Heffington as the film''s choreographer to work on the actors'' timing and movements in order to sync them with the music soundtrack.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23363, 'In 2010, Jon Hamm plays as a FBI agent investigating a heist. In this movie he plays as a member of a heist team.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23364, 'During the post office scene, the teller at the counter quotes Dolly Parton: "Everybody wants happiness, nobody wants pain, but you can''t have a rainbow without a little rain." The final heist begins in the rain. When Baby is released from prison, a rainbow is visible in the background.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23365, 'After the first bank robbery, Griff (Jon Bernthal) jokes, "If you don''t see me again, it''s because I''m dead." His character is never seen again in the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23366, 'When Baby flicks through the TV channels towards the start of the film, the dialogue from each channel teases what happens in the final heist.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23367, 'Edgar Wright said that the final scene where Baby gets out of jail was deliberately left ambiguous (notice that neither Baby nor Debora remains visibly aged) as to leave to the audience interpretation of whether he really got paroled, and as what the teller said about the rainbow turns out correct; OR it is merely a figment of his imagination. It also had both actors Ansel Elgort and Lily James divisive about it. Elgort thinks that it is indeed his imagination, while James thinks that it indeed happens.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23368, 'The numbers (28071978) on Baby''s prison jumpsuit at the end of the film correspond to the release date of The Driver (1978)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23369, 'Baby is listening to "Brighton Rock" by Queen on his iPod, which foreshadows events that later occur in the movie. The song is a reference to the story Brighton Rock by Graham Greene, in which character Pinkie is a teenager in a gang. Throughout the story, Pinkie is trying to cover his tracks of all of the murders and secrets that he''s wrapped up in. He falls in love with a girl named Rose who is a waitress at a diner. At the end of the novel, all of the crime has finally caught up to Pinkie and, after being chased by the police, he dies. The only person left standing is Rose (the love interest) from the diner.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23370, 'Despite receiving top billing, Jon Bernthal only has 5 minutes of screen time.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23371, 'In Bo''s Diner, Darling tells Bats that "when Buddy sees red, all you''ll see is black." During the final confrontation between Buddy and Baby in the parking garage, red low lights are switched on in the patrol car Buddy is driving. The bull fighting documentary shown on TV at the beginning of the film also foreshadows the events of this confrontation, with the documentary stating the bull saw red and that the bullfighter began on horseback and must finish on foot.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23372, 'During the third heist''s preparation, Baby is absentmindedly playing with a toy car when he accidentally drops it off the table. This foreshadows a scene in the third act in which Baby rams a cop car off of an upper level parking lot onto the street below.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23373, 'The man (R. Marcos Taylor) who recognized Bats in the arms deal was one of the guards Bats encountered (the other was killed) at the armored truck heist.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23374, 'Heavy amounts of foreshadowing are shown in the scene where Baby/Miles is flipping through channels on Joe''s TV. "You are so beautiful" being his first meeting with Debbie, "they grow up so freakin'' fast" being the post office scout with Doc''s nephew, "how''s that workin out for ya?" being his first meeting with JD, the Monsters Inc. scene being a line he uses on Doc twice, and the bull fighting documentary ("the bull sees nothing but red; Gaston is running out of options. He began this on horseback and must now finish it on foot") foreshadows his final confrontation with Buddy in the parking garage. Darling also refers to buddy as "relentless" and says he "sees red" in the diner while speaking to Bats.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23375, 'Body count: 14.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23376, 'Film director Walter Hill provides the voice of the courtroom interpreter. Hill directed The Driver (1978), one of Edgar Wright''s primary inspirations for this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23377, 'Following the final heist, Baby rushes home and discovers a wounded Joseph inside their ransacked apartment. Records are most notably scattered all over the place, with the most visible being the original albums from which the songs on the film''s soundtrack are taken.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23378, 'One of the antique postcards Baby receives while in prison matches the Route 66 mural in Bo''s Diner.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23379, 'Baby Driver contains quite a few references to the 1989 anime getaway driver film Riding Bean. Among them are Baby''s facial scarring (and specifically the way his upper scar sticks out above his sunglasses), the supercharged red sports car with a hood scoop he drives in the first chase scene of the film, the use of license plate numbers to refer to other car chase movies, and, hugely, the final showdown between Buddy and Baby in a parking garage, which mirrors the final sequence of Riding Bean and even includes a few nearly-identical shots.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23380, 'Earlier in the film Baby is instructed to get an Avalanche or a Tahoe, something big in case he has to run a cop car into a wall, foreshadowing the way Baby runs Buddy''s stolen cop car into a wall.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23381, 'In the movie, it''s revealed that Buddy''s real name is Jason Van Horn; it can be overhead on the police radio in the parking garage during the final showdown between Baby and Buddy.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23382, 'Buddy quotes Romeo and Juliet minutes before his death. The Shakespeare play also features in Hot Fuzz (2007).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23383, 'The film''s ending was partially inspired by the 1938 gangster film, Angels with Dirty Faces, as both feature criminals taking responsibility for their actions and being willing to face the consequences.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23384, 'J.D. dropped his gun because he is the only crew member who doesn''t have a strap on his shotgun.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23386, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23403, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23404, 'Up to 70% of Nine Lives was computer-generated.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23405, 'Mark Consuelos is allergic to cats which made filming any scenes with Mr. Fuzzypants (David) difficult. In the scene where he is struggling with the cat his reactions of disgust are real.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23406, 'There originally was a subplot involving catnip as an allegorical analogue for addiction, but it was cut for time and because executives believed it would be too much for a PG-rated children''s movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23407, 'Celebrity cat Lil Bub makes a cameo in this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23408, 'The movie was released as Mr. Fuzzypants in United Arab Emirates and Australia.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23409, 'Rated the worst film of 2016 by Metacritic critics.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23410, 'Six cast members have appeared in superhero productions. Malina Weissman played Young Kara in Supergirl (2015). Teddy Sears played Hunter Soloman/Zoom, and Robbie Amell played Ronnie Raymond/Firestorm, in The Flash (2014). Kevin Spacey played Lex Luthor in Superman Returns (2006). Jennifer Garner played Elektra in Daredevil (2003) and Elektra (2005), In Batman Returns (1992) Christopher Walken played Max Shreck.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23411, 'Tom Brand making pull ups as a cat is reference to Kevin Spacey''s another role as Lester Burnham in American Beauty (1999).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23412, 'A photo shows Tom sitting with former president George W. Bush. Kevin Spacey played President Richard Nixon in Elvis & Nixon (2016).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23413, 'The film was originally scheduled for release on April 29, 2016.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23414, 'Although asked, there is never an explanation given for ''Fire'' in the company name ''FireBrand''. One explanation could be that in the Dutch language ''Brand'' translates to ''Fire'' in English.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23416, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23417, 'Based on a true story. In December 1970, Elvis Presley met President Richard Nixon, who appointed Presley as an honorary DEA agent.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23418, 'Portraying Elvis Presley, Michael Shannon thought that the karate scene in the film was over the top.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23419, 'Eric Bana was originally cast as Elvis Presley, but he withdrew from the part.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23420, 'The real-life photograph of Elvis Presley and Richard Nixon in their early 1970s meeting is the most requested ever from the National Archives.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23421, 'Elvis Presley and Jerry Schilling used to practice karate. They even had karate names: "Mr. Tiger" and "Mr. Cougar" respectively.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23422, 'In the film''s early stage of development, this was going to be a micro-budget movie, with co-screenwriter Joey Sagal going to play Elvis Presley. However, he ended up playing Elvis Impersonator Joe King instead.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23423, 'When Jerry Schilling and Sonny meet Bud Krogh and Chapin in the parking garage, director Liza Johnson interpreted it as a reference to Watergate, which hadn''t happened yet.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23424, 'Elvis Presley and Richard Nixon don''t appear on screen together until 1:06 into the movie. The film is 1:22, so their sequence lasts about 16 minutes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23425, 'Jerry Schilling actually proof-read the letter from Elvis Presley to Richard Nixon.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23426, 'Inspired by a conversation about Elvis Presley''s badge at Cassian Elwes'' Christmas party, co-executive producer and co-screenwriter Hanala Sagal wrote a 90-page script with her now ex-husband, Joey Sagal. After their script was written, Cary Elwes asked to collaborate on the screenplay and to direct the film. Elwes did not end up directing, but did co-write the film, and is credited as a screenwriter.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23427, 'Jerry Schilling was a stand in for Elvis Presley for eight of his movies.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23428, 'Jerry Schilling met Elvis Presley when they were twelve years old at a touch football game in North Memphis, Tennessee.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23429, 'Essential to fleshing out the story were two first-hand accounts of the meeting and the events leading up to it. The memoir "Me and a Guy Named Elvis", by long-time Elvis Presley confidant Jerry Schilling, became a road map for the writers in early drafts. The handwritten notes taken during the meeting by Richard Nixon counsel Egil Bud Krogh, which he later compiled into his own account, "The Day Elvis Met Nixon", were incorporated into the final draft');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23430, 'The favorite show of Jerry Schilling, a childhood friend of Elvis Presley, was House of Cards (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23431, 'The film takes place on 21st December 1970.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23432, 'In the scene where Elvis Presley is watching multiple televisions at Graceland in Memphis, Tennessee, director Liza Johnson wanted to reflect the cultural forces at work on Elvis such as the left youth culture and anti-war culture.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23434, 'According to Jerry Schilling, he, Cary Elwes, Bud Krogh, Alex Pettyfer, and Johnny Knoxville went to a bar after filming. Bud did scenes for Cary, and Johnny lit Alex''s foot on fire with tequila.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23435, 'Kevin Spacey, who plays Richard Nixon, and Michael Shannon, who portrays Elvis Presley, have both played villains in "Superman" films: Spacey played Lex Luthor in Superman Returns (2006) while Shannon played General Zod in Man of Steel (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23436, 'In the fourth season of House of Cards (2013), Kevin Spacey''s character of Francis Joseph "Frank" Underwood, mentions that he wishes to be Richard Nixon.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23437, 'With Jerry Schilling offering Elvis Presley''s side of the story and Bud Krogh representing the White House perspective, the producers knew they had the makings of a great movie. "When I read the script I was like, ''I gotta make this movie'', said producer Cassian Elwes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23438, 'The first scene in the Oval Office was the first scene to be shot.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23439, 'The idea to make a feature film about the meeting between Elvis Presley and Richard Nixon was originally inspired by a portrait of an unsmiling Elvis, facing the camera and in profile, mugshot-style, that hangs in the home of producer Cassian Elwes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23440, 'Third filmed production about the actual real-life meeting of Elvis Presley and former American President Richard Nixon. The first two were Elvis Meets Nixon (1997) and When Elvis Met Nixon (2009). Each was made in a subsequent decade: the 1990s, the 2000s, and Elvis & Nixon (2016) in the 2010s.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23441, 'The scene where Elvis appears in the Memphis International Airport was actually filmed in the New Orleans train station.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23442, 'Cary Elwes said he would make his directional debut with the same concept of this film. Eric Bana was even rumored to play Elvis Presley.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23443, 'At a Christmas party, producer Cassian Elwes'' long-time friend, Joey Sagal, an actor who has played Elvis Presley in movies, television and on stage, explained the story behind artist Russell Young''s silk-screened artwork. "He told me the picture was taken when Elvis secretly went to Washington and became an undercover narcotics agent," recalled Elwes. "He said, ''This is the official photograph from Elvis getting the badge.'' And I go, ''What are you talking about?'' So Joey proceeded to tell the whole story. Joey then said, this is the movie we should make" Encouraged by Elwes, Sagal, who appeared as Elvis in the Steppenwolf production of ''Steve Martin''''s play "Picasso at the Lapin Agile" at the Geffen Playhouse, and his then wife, Hanala, wrote the script for Elvis & Nixon_. Cassian''s brother, actor and screenwriter Cary Elwes, later expanded the script.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23444, 'The title roles of Richard Nixon and Elvis Presley are played by stars who have both appeared in films directed by Sam Mendes and were both Oscar nominated for Acting Academy Awards for each of their performances. The actors and movies were respectively, Kevin Spacey in American Beauty (1999), who won, and Michael Shannon in Revolutionary Road (2008), who lost.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23445, 'Kevin Spacey previously appeared in Superman Returns (2006), which also featured Frank Langella, who played the part of Richard Nixon in Frost/Nixon (2008). Director Bryan Singer later included Nixon as a character in X-Men: Days of Future Past (2014).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23446, 'This film is not the first time actor Kevin Spacey, who plays former the late former American President Richard Nixon, has played the role of an American President. Spacey has also played an American President, the fictional President Francis Underwood, in Netflix''s House of Cards (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23448, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23449, 'Jason Sudeikis stated in an interview that they wanted to put a gag in the film, where Jamie Foxx''s character says to Nick, Kurt, and Dale, "You crackers got to go. I have three other crackers coming in," and as the trio get up to leave, the three characters from The Hangover movies would come in and sit at the booth. They finally decided against it, because it would take the audience out of the movie. Zach Galifianakis and Ed Helms (Alan and Stu from The Hangover film franchise) later heard about this, and thought the idea was hilarious.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23450, 'This is the first sequel Jennifer Aniston has ever done in her entire career.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23451, 'Tommy Lee Jones and Jack Nicholson were considered for the role that went to Christoph Waltz.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23452, 'Jamie Foxx and Christoph Waltz appeared in Django Unchained (2012).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23453, 'The cast has a total of five Academy awards thanks to one from Jamie Foxx (Ray (2004)), two from Kevin Spacey (The Usual Suspects (1995), American Beauty (1999)), and two from Christoph Waltz (Inglourious Basterds (2009), Django Unchained (2012)).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23454, 'The name Nick gives to Julia, Blanston, is an homage to a Steve Martin stand-up bit where he claimed his real name was Gern Blanston.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23455, 'Chris Pine''s character''s name (Rex Hanson), and several T-rex props throughout the movie are used in reference to This Means War (2012), in which is said that Chris Pine''s character, FDR Foster, has small, T-rex like, hands.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23456, 'Among the three lead stars, Charlie Day is the only actor that didn''t have Jennifer Aniston as his leading lady (Sudeikis, We''re the Millers (2013) and Bateman, The Switch (2012)).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23457, 'This film and the first one use the song "How You Like Me Now?" by The Heavy during the credits and bloopers.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23458, 'This is the fourth film Jason Sudeikis and Jennifer Aniston have done together. The others being The Bounty Hunter (2010), Horrible Bosses (2011), We''re the Millers (2013), and Mother''s Day (2016).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23459, 'The fact that Dale is constantly accused of being racist is possibly a reference to the first film, where he''s constantly accused of being a child molester.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23460, 'Second movie in 2014 that Chris Pine punches himself in the face, the other one being Stretch (2014).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23461, 'Shipped to theaters under the name "Backstab".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23462, 'In the movie, the scene where Nick and Dale walk out of the hotel wearing the hotel uniforms is almost identical to the scene in Smokin'' Aces (2006), when the Tremor brothers are entering the hotel. In Smokin'' Aces (2006), Chris Pine played Darwin Tremor.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23463, 'Jason Sudeikis and Christoph Waltz appeared in Epic (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23464, 'Jamie Foxx, Christoph Waltz, and Kevin Spacey are all Academy Award Winners.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23465, 'Jason Bateman and Jonathan Banks appeared in Identity Thief (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23466, 'Fourth collaboration with Jason Sudeikis and Charlie Day. The first three were Going the Distance (2010), Horrible Bosses (2011), and It''s Always Sunny in Philadelphia (2005).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23467, 'Kevin Spacey (Dave Harken) and Jonathan Banks (Detective Hatcher) appeared on Wiseguy (1987).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23469, 'When Nick, Kurt, and Dale are in the office arguing about "Kidnapping". You can see a schematic of the Shower Buddy on top of the table in the shape of the U.S.S. Enterprise. This is an homage to Chris Pine (Rex), who has starred in three Star Trek movies.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23470, 'All of the main characters (Dale, Nick, and Kurt) have had a sexual encounter with Julia.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23507, 'J.C. Chandor said that he wrote the script for the story he had been carrying around in his head for about a "year-and-a-half" in just four days, filling time between job interviews in Boulder, Colorado.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23472, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23474, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23508, 'John Tuld (Jeremy Irons) was originally offered to Sir Ben Kingsley, but due to other projects, he couldn''t play the role. Billy Crudup and Tim Robbins were also interested in taking parts, but had to refuse, due to other obligations.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23509, 'Grace Gummer, Meryl Streep''s third child, was set to appear in a scene in which she played Zachary Quinto''s ex-girlfriend. Due to what the director and producer called "poor directorial work" during the shoot, the scene was cut out of the film. It can be seen, however, in the "Deleted Scenes" section of the DVD.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23510, 'In one scene, John Tuld (Jeremy Irons) picks up a toy that looks like Mufasa from The Lion King (1994), a possible nod to the film, in which Irons also famously starred as Scar.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23511, 'This was Writer and Director J.C. Chandor''s first feature-length film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23478, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23480, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23481, 'To promote this film, Warner Brothers Pictures Canada set up a twelve-foot Voodoo doll resembling a corporate boss in downtown Montreal. People were given the chance to vent their office frustrations on the doll by stabbing and hitting it with large needles. They were also encouraged to share their best or worst boss story for the chance of winning passes to an advance screening of the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23482, 'Jennifer Aniston wore a brown wig to make her character a brunette and more oversexed, a departure from her usual lighter roles.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23483, 'When looking for a dangerous bar, Gregory claims there is an Applebee''s three blocks away. Jason Sudeikis says "those aren''t the shitheads we need." Sudeikis would later become the spokesman for Applebee''s.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23484, 'While Director Seth Gordon encouraged most actors and actresses to improvise their lines in various scenes, Jennifer Aniston stated she did not need to because her lines were "beautifully choreographed".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23485, 'Jason Sudeikis and Jennifer Aniston starred together again as fake husband and wife in We''re The Millers (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23486, 'The screenplay for this film was featured in the 2005 Blacklist; a list of the "most liked" unmade scripts of the year.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23487, 'Vince Vaughn, Owen Wilson, Matthew McConaughey, Dax Shepard, Ashton Kutcher, Paul Rudd, Philip Seymour Hoffman, Jeff Bridges, and Tom Cruise were all rumored for roles at some point. Kutcher was attached to play the role of Dale Arbus, while Cruise, Hoffman, and Bridges were approached by New Line Cinema for the role of Dave Harken');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23488, 'Dale (Charlie Day) mentions a funny movie that starred Danny DeVito. Charlie Day stars in the television show, It''s Always Sunny in Philadelphia (2005) with him.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23489, 'Naomi Watts and Sarah Jessica Parker were considered to play Julia.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23490, 'Ron White''s role as a police officer is presumably tongue-in-cheek. His stand-up comedy involves numerous stories of his run-ins with the law.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23491, 'Warren Sapp and Michael Strahan both auditioned for roles.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23492, 'While Stacy talks to Dr. Harris in the dental clinic, an elevator music version of Gnarls Barkley''s song "Crazy" plays.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23493, 'The glasses worn by Jennifer Aniston at the dental clinic are custom made Oakley Radar Path.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23494, 'Meghan Markle and Wendell Pierce play daughter and father on the television series Suits (2011).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23495, 'Mike McCready, the guitar player for Pearl Jam is credited as a "featured musician" on the soundtrack.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23496, 'Frank Oz and Brett Ratner were both attached to direct at some point.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23497, 'Anne Fletcher was the studio''s first choice to direct.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23498, 'Kurt is the only one out of the three main characters to come in contact with the three targeted bosses. Kurt works for Bobby Pellitt, has sexual intercourse with Dr. Julia Harris (Kurt is never seen interacting with her, just Julia opening her front door to invite Kurt into her home for sex) and is held at gunpoint, along with Nick and Dale, by Dave Harken. Nick works for Harken, he never interacts with Pellitt (though he does witness Harken murdering Pellitt), and is never seen with Julia. Dale works for Julia, is held at gunpoint by Harken, but never interacts with Pellitt. Additionally, he has interactions with Harken when Harken gets angry with him for littering, after which Dale saves his life (he didn''t know it was Harken) when he almost dies because of a peanut allergy.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23499, 'At the seedy motel, where the supposed hitman is being interviewed. When he shows up at the door, a mezuzah (a small Jewish religious case containing a prayer scroll found on the door posts of Jewish homes) is clearly seen on the doorframe.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23501, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23503, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23504, 'The film was shot in seventeen days.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23505, 'The CEO''s name, John Tuld, rhymes with the name of the ex-CEO of the now-defunct investment bank Lehman Brothers, Richard S. Fuld. Lehman Brothers, like the firm in this film, found themselves catastrophically over-leveraged in mortgage-backed-securities in the financial crisis of 2008. They eventually declared bankruptcy, and Richard Fuld was heavily criticized for his involvement in these events.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23506, 'The Moundsville Bridge mentioned by Eric Dale (Stanley Tucci) actually exists. It was completed in 1986, which would have been twenty-two years before the debt crash of 2008, which is the subject of this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23517, 'While "John Tuld" in the movie is reported to have made eighty-six million dollars in 2007, Dick Fuld, the real-life CEO of Lehman Brothers at the time, and John Thain, the real-life CEO of Merrill Lynch, the two people on which the Tuld character was based, made four million dollars and eighty-three million dollars, respectively, as a matter of "public record", and between 2000 and 2007, Fuld accumulated over five hundred twenty-nine million dollars.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23518, 'Despite prominent billing, Mary McDonnell only appears in one scene at the end of the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23520, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23521, 'The real life Susan Schmidt played Jack''s secretary in this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23522, 'Jack pitches a movie idea to Hollywood movie executives. It is a movie about Moses leading his people out of Egypt, and Jack wants Russell Crowe to star and thinks he can get Ridley to direct. 4 years later, Ridley Scott directed "Exodus: Gods and Kings", but it starred Christian Bale and not Crowe.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23523, 'The dramatic cinema movie Casino Jack (2010) and the feature film documentary Casino Jack and the United States of Money (2010), which were both pictures about the same subject, both actually debuted and premiered in the same year of 2010.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (23524, 'The license plate ''788 KCI'' is used twice for a taxi and later for Jack Abraham''s private car.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24635, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24637, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24638, 'Danny DeVito and David Marguiles have been best friends since childhood.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24640, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24642, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24643, 'Thanks to Liam Neeson''s popularity with past action hits, the film was already in profit before release, thanks to robust sales at film markets.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24644, 'Ruth Wilson was cast as Jo Durkin (who is a male character in the books), and filmed all of her scenes as Liam Neeson''s partner. But, Director Scott Frank felt that Neeson''s character should be a loner, so all of Wilson''s scenes were cut.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24645, 'The name of all three murdered women are allusions to the figure of Jesus Christ: Gotteskind (Marie Gotteskind, played by Marielle Heller, meaning "Child of God" as pointed out by T.J. (Astro); Andersen (Leila Andersen, played by Laura Birn), meaning "Son of Man"; and Kristo (Carrie Kristo, played by Razane Jammal), from which the title "Christ" derives.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24646, 'Second appearance of character Matt Scudder. The first time, it was played by Jeff Bridges in 8 Million Ways to Die (1986).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24647, 'Originally, this was supposed to be Joe Carnahan''s directorial follow up to his indie hit Narc (2002). At that time, Harrison Ford was attached to star.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24648, 'The novel, on which it is based, is number ten in the series of Matt Scudder novels by Lawrence Block. As of 2013, there are seventeen novels by this author about the character, the latest published in 2011.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24649, 'The opening scene (pre-credits) would''ve had to have taken place on May 2, 1991, assuming the newspaper that Matt (Neeson) picks up off the bar is the current edition. The headline reads that Nolan Ryan threw his seventh no-hitter. That event happened on May 1, 1991.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24650, 'Dan Stevens lost thirty pounds for his role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24651, 'In the book, the names of the brothers were Kenan and Peter Khoury, and were of Lebanese descent. The names were changed in the movie to match the more American characters, to Kenny and Peter Kristo.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24652, 'At the end, in the final scene, you can see the World Trade Center Twin Towers in the background.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24653, 'Liam Neeson and Boyd Holbrook would share the screen one more time in Run All Night (2015).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24654, 'There are two separate scenes which show the New York City skyline. The first is a panoramic view showing, from right to left, the Chrysler Building and the Empire State Building. At the end of the film, a similar skyline is shown, but shows both towers of the World Trade Center. The first view does not, despite the film taking place between 1991 and 1999. The World Trade Center was not destroyed until September 11, 2001.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (24655, 'Ben Foster was considered for the parts of both brothers (Kenny and Peter). Unfortunately, due to filming conflicts from The Program (2015), and a confirmed report that the Casting Director and producers were leaning towards Ben playing the smaller role of Peter, he decided to stick to The Program (2015), as the star of the movie. When Ben was asked about if it was him being the star compared to a limited scene, smaller co-star role in Tombstones, Ben joked "No fu*king sh*t Sherlock!" But did say he was willing to do both, only if he got to play the smaller role of Peter, so he didn''t have to worry about scheduling conflicts and not working as much. They ended up choosing Boyd Holbrook over Foster, and he immediately pulled out.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25315, 'Heather Matarazzo turned down a possibility the reprise her role of Dawn Wiener from Welcome to the Dollhouse (1995). She was replaced by Greta Gerwig.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25260, 'Is the first Live Action Reboot of a Disney Animated Feature Film that''s completely original and not an adaption of anything.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25164, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25166, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25283, 'Shakira, Joan Cusack, Drew Barrymore, Tina Fey, Uma Thurman, Gwen Stefani, Gwyneth Paltrow, Kate Beckinsale, Mindy Kaling, Shania Twain, Carrie Underwood, and Miranda Lambert were all once considered for the role of Zoe.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25168, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25170, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25172, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25302, 'Danny De Vito and Patti Lupone also played husband and wife in the film Wise Guys(1986).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25316, 'Brie Larson had filmed a scene for the film, but it was deleted from the final cut.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25259, 'There are no talking animals in this adaptation as in Dumbo (1941); instead the story is revised to include more human characters, focusing more so on their perspective.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25317, 'According to director Todd Solondz, the title character was portrayed by four dachshund show dogs but personally found them to be "dumb".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25318, 'Keaton Nigel Cooke learned "Clair De Lune" by Debussy on flute for a scene in less than one week.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25247, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25248, 'This is Danny DeVito''s fourth collaboration with Tim Burton after Batman Returns (1992), Mars Attacks! (1996) and Big Fish (2003). In three of them he has played a circus member.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25249, 'This is Eva Green''s third collaboration with Tim Burton after Dark Shadows (2012) and Miss Peregrine''s Home for Peculiar Children (2016).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25250, 'Will Smith and Tom Hanks were approached for roles. Smith was interested but backed out to do Bad Boys for Life and would later sign on for Aladdin (2019). Hanks was courted for a villain role, but turned it down to do Greyhound.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25251, 'This is Tim Burton''s first live-action remake of a Disney animated film. Alice in Wonderland (2010) is completely different from the 1950s Animated Film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25252, 'Chris Pine was offered a part, but turned it down.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25253, 'This is Michael Keaton''''s fourth collaboration with ''Tim Burton'' after Beetlejuice (1988), Batman (1989), and Batman Returns (1992).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25254, 'This is Danny DeVito''s second Disney film after Hercules (1997).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25255, 'Based off Tim Burton''s other previous interpretation of past existing, remake material, this is expected to be a darker, more serious tone and take on the Disney original classic.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25256, 'Michael Keaton and Danny DeVito previously appeared together in Johnny Dangerously (1984) and Batman Returns (1992). In both films, Keaton was the protagonist and DeVito played a villain. Here, Keaton is the villain and DeVito plays a supporting character.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25257, 'Released on Dumbo (1941)''s 78th Anniversary.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25258, 'This is Michael Keaton''s fifth Disney film, after Herbie Fully Loaded (2005), Cars (2006), Toy Story 3 (2010) and Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25261, 'This is the second collaboration between Tim Burton and Alan Arkin, with the first being Edward Scissorhands (1990).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25262, 'Will Smith declining to star in this film and instead choosing to appear in Aladdin (2019) makes him the second actor to choose a live-action remake of a Disney Renaissance over a live-action adaptation of a Walt Disney cartoon. Emma Watson was offered to play the titular character in Cinderella (2015) but chose to play Belle in Beauty and the Beast (2017) instead.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25263, 'Both Colin Farrell and Michael Keaton have played Marvel Comics villains: Farrell as Bullseye in Daredevil (2003) and Keaton as Vulture in Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25264, 'This is the 2nd Live Action Reboot of a Disney Animated Feature Film to discard the spoken dialogue of the animal characters. The first had been _Cinderella (2015)_ with the Title Character''s Mouse Friends.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25265, 'A code name for this movie was Big Ears.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25266, 'Is the 3rd Live Action Reboot of a Disney Animated Feature Film to release in March, after _Cinderella (2015)_ and Beauty and the Beast (2017).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25268, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25270, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25271, 'According to Arnold Schwarzenegger''s 2012 biography, Total Recall, Julius and Vincent Benedict discover they had another brother who also came from the experiment. The other brother is played by Eddie Murphy.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25319, 'Keaton Nigel Cooke is the only lead actor with two movies in this year''s Sundance Film Festival (2016).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25361, 'Dr. Seuss'' widow ended up loving what Illumination Entertainment had done so much, that she gave the rights to them to continue making films based on the books.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25273, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25274, 'Justin Timberlake, Jason Bateman, Joseph Gordon-Levitt, Jimmy Fallon, Ryan Reynolds, Neil Patrick Harris, Bryan Cranston, and Jason Segel were all considered for the role of Owen.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25275, 'Leads Emily Blunt and John Krasinski, who play a married couple, Zoe and Owen, are married in real-life as well.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25276, 'Animal Crackers is based off of a graphic novel that co-Director Scott Christian Sava wrote for his two children.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25277, 'Kaley Cuoco was originally slated to play Zoe, but due to scheduling issues, she was replaced with Emily Blunt.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25278, 'This is the fourth animated feature, for which Sylvester Stallone has provided a voice.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25279, 'Jeff Bridges, Al Pacino, Kurt Russell, Kevin Spacey, John Lithgow, Sir Patrick Stewart, Willem Dafoe, Kelsey Grammer, Mark Hamill, and Michael Douglas were all once considered for the role of Horatio.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25280, 'Dwayne Johnson was once considered for the role of Bullet-Man.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25281, 'Maya Rudolph, Nicki Minaj, Rashida Jones, Keke Palmer, and Taraji P. Henson were all once considered for the role of Binkley.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25282, 'Mel Brooks, Billy Crystal, Nathan Lane, Jim Carrey, Sir Michael Caine, Morgan Freeman, Christopher Walken, and Martin Short were all once considered for the role of Chesterfield.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25286, 'Patrick Warburton''s second time voicing an animated character by the name of "Brock", the first being bodyguard "Brock Samson" in the animated show The Venture Bros. (2003).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25287, 'James Arnold Taylor and Sylvester Stallone previously starred together in Ratchet & Clank (2016).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25288, 'Robin Williams was initially cast as Chesterfield, but his death resulted in Danny DeVito being cast. DeVito had previously directed Williams in Death to Smoochy (2002).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25290, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25291, 'When Sean Penn was on-board to direct the movie, Kristen Wiig was cast in the lead role. She was later replaced by Jennifer Aniston. However, Aniston later dropped out due to scheduling conflicts and Leslie Mann was cast.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25292, 'Robert De Niro has been trying to make this movie for 8 years.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25293, 'De Niro was trained by comedian Jessica Kirson and adopted one of her signature ''moves'': talking to herself sotto voce while turned away from the audience. He didn''t take the move quite as far, preferring to cover his face with his hand while turning slightly to one side. Kirson appears in the film longer than any other standup comic, but she is not shown using this technique.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25294, 'The Comedian is the first movie Robert De Niro and Danny De Vito have appeared in together.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25295, 'The second movie in which Robert De Niro will play a comedian. The other movie was The King of Comedy.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25296, 'Filmed in 27 days with very long filming hours. The wedding scene was filmed around 3 AM.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25297, 'Sean Penn and Mike Newell both considered directing this movie at different times.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25298, 'The seventh film featuring Robert De Niro and Harvey Keitel. They previously starred together in "Mean Streets", "Taxi Driver", "Falling in Love", "Copland" "The Bridge of San Luis Rey"and "Little Fockers", The ninth film if their "voice only" roles in "Arthur and the Minimoys"and "Dear America: Letters from Vietnam" are taken into account.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25299, 'For the screenplay, Art Linson and Richard LaGravenese wrote the drama while Jeff Ross and Lewis Friedman wrote the comedy routines.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25300, 'At the beginning of the film Jackie is seen going from Penn Station out to Long Island where he enters Governors Comedy club. This is the club that Judd Apatow, Leslie Mann''s husband in real life, performed at the beginning of his career. In Jackies character makes fun of Hicksville NY. This is a real town and is next to Syosset the town Apatow grew up in.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25301, 'Robert De Niro portrays an "insult comic", not unlike Don Rickles. De Niro and Rickles starred together in "Casino" (1995).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25304, 'At one point it was hoped that Martin Scorsese would direct the film. However, this did not come to pass.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25305, 'In October 2016, Sony Pictures Classics acquired U.S distribution rights to the film, with plans to release the film in December, in order to qualify for awards.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25306, 'The film opened to negative reviews from critics.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25307, 'In North America, The Comedian was released alongside Rings and The Space Between Us, and was projected to gross $1-3 million from about 800 theaters in its opening weekend. It ended up debuting to just $892,021, finishing 21st at the box office.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25308, 'Danny DeVito''s real-life daughter Lucy DeVito plays his daughter in the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25309, 'Robert De Niro and Charles Grodin appeared before together in the 1988 classic action comedy Midnight Run, which launched Robert De Niro''s comedic career. Lois Smith also appeared in both films.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25310, 'Robert De Niro, Harvey Keitel and Edie Falco appeared in Copland (1997)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25311, 'The film had its world premiere at the AFI Fest on November 11, 2016 and was released on December 9, 2016, by Sony Pictures Classics.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25313, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25314, 'Following an angry response from some audience members at the January 2016 Sundance premiere, a few festival reviewers purposefully spoiled the film in detail so as to deter animal lovers from seeing the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25362, 'The second fully CGI animated film based on a Dr. Seuss book, the first being Horton Hears a Who! (2008).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25320, 'Wiener-Dog has won the Best Film Award at the 2017 LongTake Interative Film Festival #LIFF2017 in Milan, Italy, July 7-9. Films in competition are selected from titles yet unreleased in Italian movie theaters. The winner is chosen by people attending the screenings.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25321, 'At the Sundance premiere, the final gory segment of the movie in which the dog is repeatedly run over in the street garnered a large walkout with booing from the festival audience with just minutes left in the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25323, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25325, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25326, 'Chloë Grace Moretz was originally cast but she dropped out due to scheduling conflicts with Kick-Ass 2. She was replaced with Isabelle Fuhrman.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25327, 'Isabelle Fuhrman and Evan Ross both appear in The Hunger Games Trilogy however they act in two different films. Isabelle in The Hunger Games and Evan In The Hunger Games: Mockingjay Part 1 & 2.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25329, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25331, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25332, 'Actress Carla Gugino is the girlfriend of director Sebastian Gutierrez and appears in many of his projects.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25334, 'Reunites Robert Forster with Carla Gugino after Karen Sisco (2003) and reunites the two of them with Cameron Richardson after Rise: Blood Hunter (2007)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25335, 'Both Rosario Dawson and Carla Gunino previously worked together in 2005''s Sin City, which is almost exactly the same title name as this movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25336, 'Both Malin Akerman and Carla Gugino have previously worked together on two movies, Elektra Luxx and Watchmen. Carla Gugino played Malin Akerman''s mom on Watchmen.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25337, 'Malin Akerman previously starred in a TV show in 2015 with a title very similar to this movie''s title, Sin City Saints.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25338, 'The character name of "Eugene Portland" would seem to be an obvious reference to the second and first largest cities in Oregon.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25340, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25342, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25343, 'Danny DeVito reprised the voice of The Lorax for the Spanish, Russian, Italian, and German dubbed versions.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25344, 'Unlike the original book, the Once-ler is shown fully in the story as a human. Executive producer Christopher Meledandri said of the change, "The minute you make the Once-ler a monster, you allow the audience to interpret that the problem is caused by somebody who is different from me, and it ceases to be a story that is about all of us. Then it''s a story about, ''Oh I see, the person who led us into the predicament is not a person. It''s somebody very, very different.'' And so it takes you off the hook."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25345, 'The film premiered on March 2, 2012 - Dr. Seuss''s 108th birthday.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25346, 'Whilst playing board games with the family, Grammy Norma can make the word "Lorax" with the scrabble balls she has.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25347, 'The characters of Ted and Audrey are named after Dr. Seuss (whose real name was Theodor Seuss Geisel) and his second wife Audrey Geisel.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25348, 'This film is the first interpretation of the story to put a face to the Once-ler. In the book and the original cartoon, the Once-ler is only depicted from the arms down.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25349, 'The original name of the town in the movie is Greenville (as can be seen in the scene where the Once-ler is selling his thneeds in the town center, "Greenville Circle") before the commercial success of the product changed the name to Thneedville.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25350, 'After the success of Horton Hears a Who! (2008), Audrey Geisel, Dr Seuss'' widow, approached Illumination''s head Christopher Meledandri and said she wanted to do The Lorax next.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25351, 'The film boasts more than seventy product integration deals, a rather high number considering the ecological message that the film imparts. One of the partnerships, with Mazda, was particularly singled out for being ill-judged.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25352, 'When the Once-ler is walking to his office once he became rich, what appears to be a blow-up magazine cover is hanging on the wall. It is caption "Too big to fail", which is a colloquial term in economics to define an institution whose failure would bring catastrophic consequences to the economy. After the 2009 banking collapse, modern economists have said that institutions too big to fail are simply too big to exist.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25353, 'Ed Helms voices both the young, and old versions of the Once-ler.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25354, 'When the characters are throwing money toward the Once-ler when they begin to love his invention, the money has the Mayor of Whoville''s face on it.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25355, 'This is the first film to feature Universal''s 100th Anniversary logo.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25356, 'In the original 1972 animated version, The Once-ler was never sympathetic to the Lorax, before the last Truffula tree fell. Differing from this film, where Once-ler and the Lorax were friends.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25357, 'As Ted gathers everything to see the Once-ler, there is a Minion figure from Despicable Me (2010) in Ted''s drawer.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25358, 'At the movie''s premiere, Zac Efron dropped a condom on the ground during picture taking.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25359, 'The first film from Illumination to be given an IMAX 3-D release (or IMAX Tree-D as the publicity called it).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25360, 'The logo on Ted''s shoes say "Gru''s Shoes" on the sides of them.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25366, 'Although they go uncredited because they have no lines of dialogue at all in the movie, O''Hare''s henchmen are called Buddy and McGirt. O''Hare calls them by name only once, when he orders them to search Ted''s room for the Truffula seed. Together, they are named after retired champion boxer James Walter "Buddy" McGirt, who during his boxing career was the IBF light-welterweight champion, and Lineal and WBC welterweight champion.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25367, 'Argentinian film Producer Axel Kuschevatzky dubbed Mr. O''Hare on the Latin American Spanish speaking prints of the movie.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25368, 'Jenny Slate''s first animated film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25369, 'This is Danny DeVito''s fifth animated film, after My Little Pony: The Movie (1986), _Look Who''s Talking Now (1991)_, Space Jam (1996), and Hercules (1997).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25370, 'When Ted opens his bed side table, a mini minion figurine can be seen.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25371, 'First Theatrically released Dr. Seuss film to be Rated PG by the MPAA.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25372, 'If O''Hare was able to seal the door to the city, how was Ted able to get back into the city after visiting the Once-ler the third time?');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25373, 'Rob Riggle voices the young and old versions of Mr. O''Hare.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25374, 'The pollution scene marks a connection to factories in the Industrial Revolution pollution controversy.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25375, 'Ed Helms 2nd Animated film, after Monsters vs. Aliens (2009).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25376, 'From the Creators of "Despicable Me".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25377, 'Illumination''s only Dr. Seuss film that''s not a reboot of a previous film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25378, 'This is Illumination''s first musical film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25379, 'Illumination''s third feature film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25380, 'The soundtrack reflects the natural vs. man-made nature of the scene. For example, the opening song "Thneedville" describes the thoroughly artificial town with completely electronic music. Meanwhile, the finale "Let It Grow" and the planting of an all-natural tree is made with almost all acoustic instruments. "Let It Grow" even includes a capella choral music (with no man-made instruments at all).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25381, 'Despite being a singer by trade, Taylor Swift doesn''t sing in the final song (Let it grow).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25412, 'Although it might appear otherwise, one of the more enthusiastic participants in the film who was in on the joke was Sean Combs. He only had to have one meeting with Joaquin Phoenix and Casey Affleck to agree to take part. All his scenes were improvised.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25383, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25384, 'Shot in eleven days with a Canon 7D camera.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25385, 'Sebastian Gutierrez claimed at the South by Southwest Film Festival premiere of Elektra Luxx (2010) that Girl Walks Into a Bar (2011) is the first feature length film with a cast of notable stars made expressly for the Internet.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25386, 'Inspired by a scene from Elektra Luxx (2010).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25387, 'Alexis Bledel, Rosario Dawson, Carla Gugino, and Josh Hartnett also appeared in Sin City (2005).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25389, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25391, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25393, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25394, 'In September 2010, co-Screenwriter and Director Casey Affleck confirmed that this movie is not a real documentary, but fake. The public had been wondering, ever since Joaquin Phoenix announced in October 2008 his retirement from acting, in order to become a rapper, whether it was all just an act, or if it was for real.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25395, 'The idea for the film came from Joaquin Phoenix''s amazement at the way people believed that reality television shows were unscripted. By claiming to retire from acting, he and his brother-in-law Casey Affleck planned to make a film that "explored celebrity, and explored the relationship between the media and the consumers, and the celebrities themselves".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25396, 'Directorial debut of Casey Affleck.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25397, 'Effectively, Joaquin Phoenix played this variation of himself for two whole years. Some critics have argued that it is one of his greatest, most sustained performances.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25398, 'The movie that Ben Stiller pitches to Joaquin Phoenix is Greenberg (2010), with Stiller angling for Phoenix to play the part of Ivan. That part was actually played by Rhys Ifans. This is all part of the joke, however, as Greenberg (2010) was already being filmed, when Stiller showed up in this scene. Indeed, this scene was filmed after the David Letterman interview, and Stiller''s appearance at the Oscars, dressed as Joaquin.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25400, 'The first hint that Joaquin Phoenix was going to pull a stunt like this, came in October 2008, when he announced his retirement on the red carpet of his film Two Lovers (2008), which he then proclaimed to be his final performance. (Ironically, Phoenix got some of the best reviews of his career for his performance in the film.)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25401, 'In the defecation scene, where Joaquin Phoenix gets pooped on in bed, the "feces" was actually a combination of humus and coffee grounds. The mixture was inserted into a tube that was taped onto Antony Langdon''s (Anton''s) back that went down to his butt.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25402, 'Phoenix originally conceived of the idea after he became fascinated by the show Celebrity Rehab with Dr. Drew, and in fact, originally attempted to execute the stunt by being featured on the show. However, Phoenix ditched this idea, when he realized it would be cruel to be performing a character amongst people with very real problems.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25403, 'Some of the soundbites from entertainment journalists are made up.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25404, 'The defecation scene required approximately thirty-five takes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25405, 'Magnolia Pictures were rather annoyed with the whole set-up, as they were trying to publicize Two Lovers (2008), with a star that refused to be interviewed, and who yet was being followed by a documentary crew at all times. They believed that Phoenix''s "stunt" took a lot of attention away from James Gray''s well-received film, which was a box-office flop.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25406, 'In September 2010, Casey Affleck was sued for sexual harassment by Producer Amanda White and Cinematographer Magdalena Górka. The incidents supposedly occurred during their work together on this movie. The cases were settled.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25407, 'In 2016, while a guest on the National Public Radio program "Fresh Air," Casey Affleck said that filming one of the scenes in this movie was the occasion for one of the only conversations of any length or depth between Casey Affleck and his father, Tim Affleck, about the debilitating alcoholism that the elder Affleck had struggled with during much of Casey''s early childhood. Tim Affleck, who played Joaquin Phoenix''s character''s father, had been sober for many decades when he shot the scene, in which Phoenix is supposed to have traveled to Costa Rica to visit his "father"; Casey Affleck set the scene at a bar, "and I put a beer in front of my dad. And I was not intending for him to drink the beer. I just wanted him to be--both of the characters just to be sitting there in silence, sort of uncomfortable silence between father and son. And my dad looked at me and he said, ''I can''t drink this.'' I said, ''I know you can''t, dad. You don''t--I (don''t) want you to drink--for God''s sake, don''t drink. And that''s probably the only time we talked about his recovery and sobriety since - since he got sober. You know, he doesn''t talk about it much. But he is a lovable guy, and I have a great relationship with him. He''s really very, very smart. And it''s been - you know, I got to know a whole new person when I was a teenager because the man I knew before that was just completely different. So in some ways, I kind of began my relationship with the father I know now when I was a teenager."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25408, 'In the scene where Anton is playing the piano and singing a song (the scene between calling the prostitutes and them actually coming), the shot in the film was actually the third take. Also, the song being sung was written by Anton''s brother, and he (Anton) is singing it in a different pitch in the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25409, 'The sixth film featuring Jack Nicholson and Danny DeVito.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25410, 'Towards the end of the movie, there is a scene where Joaquin Phoenix is sitting with his father, at a table, drinking beers. In reality, this man is not Joaquin Phoenix''s father, but actually Casey Affleck and Ben Affleck''s own real-life father.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25411, 'Joaquin Phoenix possesses the unique ability to make himself throw up without even having to stick his fingers down his throat. This gift came in handy for the scene after his disastrous rap performance where he is seen barfing into a toilet.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25413, 'Edward James Olmos'' seemingly off-the-cuff motivational speech to Joaquin Phoenix was entirely scripted by Casey Affleck.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25414, 'Affleck and Phoenix''s production company is called They Are Going to Kill Us Productions, an indication that the whole thing is a stunt.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25415, 'The final sequence in the film, where Joaquin Phoenix is trekking through the river, was actually longer in the original cut. It was almost another three minutes longer, but Casey Affleck thought that it was "beating a dead horse" at that point, and decided to cut it shorter, and that is what we see in the final film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25416, 'The lyrical end shot where Joaquin Phoenix walks off into a river took three takes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25418, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25419, 'Dax Shepard appears as one of Kristen Bell''s would-be suitors. He would later become her real life husband.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25420, 'After her return from Rome Beth receives a phone call from Joan, informing her that she is "front page news" due to her climbing into the Fountain of Love. A cutaway shows a newspaper with the headline "Stupidissima". This translates not simply as "stupid", but rather as "the pinnacle of stupidity".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25421, 'While standing in the Fountain of Love at the beginning of the Film, Beth looks down at the coins and though she''s in Rome, most of the change is in US currency.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25422, 'The scenes in the Guggenheim Museum were filmed during an actual exhibition by Cai Guo-Qiang called "I Want To Believe": The cars in the main entrance suspended from the roof was a piece entitled "Inopportune: Stage One"; The tigers with arrows protruding from them is "Inopportune: Stage Two"; The taxidermy wolves (which the coin rolls between as Beth runs after it) is a piece entitled "Head On".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25423, 'Jon Heder''s character, a goth street magician, is a parody of famous illusionist Criss Angel (in both looks and magic tricks performed)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25424, 'The gallery''s final "main" piece, "a photo by Petruccelli entitled ''The Hit''", was named after the movie''s Production Designer, Kirk M. Petruccelli.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25425, 'People throwing coins into the Fontana di Trevi, the reputed Fountain of Love in Rome to have their wishes granted in matters of the heart is true; in fact, it''s an offense to try to steal coins from the fountain because it''s the same as stealing other people''s wishes.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25426, 'In the last movie with Jon Heder and Efren Ramirez (Napoleon Dynamite (2004)), the song "The Promise" was featured prominently. That song was performed by the band "When in Rome."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (25427, 'Bill Hader was considered for the role of Nick.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26630, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26631, '7''54 standing ovation at Cannes Film Festival 2015.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26632, 'When writing the script, Nanni Moretti used what he had written during his mother''s sickness.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26633, 'In the dream scene at the cinema, the crowd is in line for Wings of Desire (1987).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26634, 'The scene in which John Turturro''s character Barry expresses his frustration at driving in a car that''s so laden with cameras he can''t see out didn''t require much acting from Turturro. He found the rigors of driving in such a car (a stick shift which he wasn''t used to), unable to see out properly, all whilst trying to speak in Italian to be quite overwhelming.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26635, 'The title of the film that Margherita is shooting is "Noi siamo qui" (We Are Here).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26636, 'According to Nanni Moretti, the real autobiographical aspect of the film ''is the feeling that Margherita has - that she never feels up to what she''s doing, that she''s always ill at ease''.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26637, 'Much of John Turturro''s performance was improvised.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26638, 'Chosen by the Cahiers du Cinéma as the best picture of 2015.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26639, 'This won Margherita Buy her 5th David di Donatello Best Actress award (the Italian equivalent of the Oscars).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26640, 'Nanni Moretti wrote the lead role with Margherita Buy in mind.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26641, 'In Spain was only released in 46 theaters / Widest release: 48 theaters.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26642, 'The film parallels writer/director/actor Nanni Moretti''s own life. Like his mother, Agata, died in 2010 as Moretti was finishing Habemus Papam; his mother Agata was a teacher of classical languages (Latin and Greek). Also the car Margherita drives is Moretti''s; his parents'' books line the walls of the film''s interiors; and Giulia Lazzarini, who plays Margherita''s mother, wears clothes Agata wore in hospital.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26643, 'The most moving moment for Nanni Moretti while making Mia Madre is the scene where the granddaughter overhears a phone call in which she hears her grandmother has passed away, she understands what has happened and she just hides under the blanket.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26645, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26647, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26649, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26730, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26769, 'Camila Pitanga''s scenes as John Turturro''s character''s lover in "Quando não há Mais Amor" were cut for unknown reasons.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26739, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26741, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26743, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26744, 'After seeing the film for the first time, Sir Michael Caine wrote Writer and Director Paolo Sorrentino a letter, saying he was deeply touched, and he described how, during the trip back home in the taxi with his wife, he kept on crying.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26745, 'Paolo Sorrentino wrote the script with Sir Michael Caine in mind as the main character.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26746, 'Sir Michael Caine was given dark-framed glasses to wear "because they would make my hair appear to be whiter."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26747, 'Jane Fonda became interested in the role of Brenda, after friend Al Pacino had told her that the part was "written for you." Another actress had been cast, but dropped out, and so Fonda had her agent secure the role on her behalf.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26748, 'Singers Paloma Faith, Mark Kozelek (Sun Kil Moon), and Sumi Jo all play themselves in the movie with Faith having a speaking part as well.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26749, 'With the film, Paolo Sorrentino hoped that he have explored what is to come; his future as an old man.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26750, 'The movie is shot in the eastern part of the Swiss Alps. There is a shot in the movie, of the train station of Wiesen. This village is located between St. Moritz and Davos.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26751, 'Madalina Diana Ghenea, who is playing Miss Universe in the film, was 26 at the time of filming. In real-life, she would''ve been the oldest Miss Universe ever (sharing this honor with 1997 American winner Brook Mahealani Lee).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26752, 'The particular inception point of the film was the story of Riccardo Muti being invited by the Queen to conduct a concert. Because they could not agree on the repertoire, Muti turned the Queen down, which was something Paolo Sorrentino wrote in his diary and was later inspired by.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26753, 'Madalina Diana Ghenea''s famous scene in the bath was Number 1 in WhatCulture.com''s "15 Most Paused Movie Moments Of 2015": "So gob-smacking, was this nude scene in Paolo Sorrentino''s Youth - La giovinezza (2015), that it ended up being used as the film''s official poster, despite the fact that the scene is a minor part of the film. And of course the fact that no mainstream cinema in the world would be able to display it, for fear of inciting prudish parents. But you can see why they did it: casting Romanian model-turned-actress Madalina Diana Ghenea to play Miss Universe for the nude scene was an inspired choice. As adverts for the beauty of the human body go, there''s no denying she''s pretty compelling." (Simon Gallagher, 2015)');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26754, 'According to Paolo Sorrentino, the character of filmmaker Mick (Harvey Keitel), is far from being an autobiographical creation, and is a fairly non-specific filmmaker - "a little bit of Roger Corman, a bit of Sidney Lumet, a bit of William Friedkin".');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26755, 'The film cast includes three Oscar winners: Sir Michael Caine, Jane Fonda, and Rachel Weisz; and one Oscar nominee: Harvey Keitel.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26756, 'The movie is dedicated to the memory of the great Italian director Francesco Rosi (1922-2015).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26757, 'In the scene where "Maradona" wonders while having his foot massaged by his assistant, he imagines profiling the National teams of Argentina and England, with the same uniforms of the famous confrontation the Mexico''s 1986 World Cup. In this match, Maradona scored two of his most memorable goals throughout his career.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26758, 'The first film to be picked up by Fox Searchlight at the Cannes Film Festival.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26759, 'The final scene''s look, in which Fred Ballinger (Sir Michael Caine) conducts his piece, is heavily reminiscent of Federico Fellini''s "Orchestra Rehearsal". Fellini is a huge influence on Sorrentino.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26761, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26763, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26765, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26766, 'Marcelo Serrado had to escalate the Sugarloaf Mountain along with Ryan Kwanten for the "Acho que Estou Apaixonado" segment, though he is afraid of heights. He ended up using the help of steel cables to be lift up which were removed during post-production.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26767, 'José Padilha''s segment "Inútil Paisagem" was almost cut from the theatrical release due to legal threats from religious institutions because of the use of the Christ statue''s image and its context. They first considered it to be offensive and disrespectful, though later backed off.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26770, 'Stephan Elliott wrote his segment based on his own life story, where he met his partner in the same circumstances.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26771, 'The inspiration behind John Turturro''s segment was taken from a song by Vanessa Paradis, who also stars in the short.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26772, 'Cauã Antunes''s film and acting debut.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26773, 'Live action directorial debut of Carlos Saldanha.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26774, 'Hugo Carvana''s final role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26776, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26777, 'One of Sorrentino''s inspirations for this movie was Flaubert''s famous statement that he intended to write a novel about nothing. Sorrentino stated, "By ''nothing'' he meant the rumors and gossip, the thousand ways we have of wasting time, the things that irritate us or delight us but that are so short-lived that they make us doubt the meaning of life. That ''nothing'' makes up many people''s entire lives." He also said that he wanted to depict "the great thing about life, the fact that you can be surprised by something that you''d decided was vulgar and wretched, and then suddenly what is vulgar and wretched reveals its own entirely unexpected grace."');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26778, 'The character of Talia Concept is an obvious reference to artist Marina Abramovic.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26779, 'In an interview conducted by the Italian radio station Radio 2, Paolo Sorrentino claimed that, at some point during production, he was considering to call the film "L''Apparato Umano". "L''Apparato Umano" also is the title of the fictional novel written by the protagonist of the film, Jep Gambardella, played by Toni Servillo.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26780, 'The first cut of the movie was 183-minute long.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26781, 'Italy''s official submission to the Best Foreign Language Film category for the 86th Academy Awards; the other six films considered were: Midway - Tra la vita e la morte (2013), Miele (2013), Razza bastarda (2012), Salvo (2013), Viaggio sola (2013), and Viva la libertà (2013).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26782, 'During a conversation, Jep says, "Who am I? There is a novel that begins like this." That novel is André Breton''s "Nadja" (1928). The central part of the movie, which deals with the relationship between Jep and Ramona, draws extensively from Breton''s novel.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26783, 'Dedicated to the famous Italian rugby player and journalist Giuseppe D''Avanzo - good friends with the director Paolo Sorrentino - who passed away during the production of the film.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26784, 'At around 1 hr 20 mins, one can see the famous sculpture The Dying Gaul, or Galata Morente, from the neck up for a few seconds.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26785, 'Francesco Rosi, who is friend with Paolo Sorrentino, directed the conclave scene. Sorrentino makes a cameo in the scene and he did not want to direct himself.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26786, 'Included among the "1001 Movies You Must See Before You Die", edited by Steven Schneider.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26787, 'Egidio (nightclub mgr.; Ramona''s father): "She can''t be a stripper at 50." At time of production, she was closer to 50 than 42.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26788, 'During the arrest scene, Jep Gambardella discovers that his mysterious and well-dressed neighbor is called Moneta and that he works for an organization that "keeps Italy going". Being ''moneta'' the Italian word for ''coin'', the neighbor is clearly based upon the real-life Cosa Nostra boss Matteo Messina Denaro (whose family name - ''Denaro'' - is the Italian word for ''money''). As of May 2010, Denaro ranked among the ten most wanted fugitives in the world, according to Forbes magazine.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26790, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26792, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26793, 'The organ-like instrument that David Byrne plays for Cheyenne is a variation of Byrne''s "house organ." Byrne created the organ in 2008 as part of an art installation project in New York City. Instead of playing musical notes, each key on the organ transmits a signal through a wire, which in turn "plays" the building: for example, motors vibrating a set of metal girders, hoses blowing air through the building''s water pipes, or metal rods striking the radiator.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26794, 'When Cheyenne is talking with David Byrne, he reveals he lives tortured by the suicide of two teens who were fans of him. This is a recreation of a real-life incident that happened in 1985 in Reno, where two young ones called Raymond Belknap and James Vance made a suicide pact after listening to Judas Priest''s songs.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26795, '''This Must Be the Place'' was originally the title for Sam Mendes summer comedy Away We Go (2009).');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26796, 'The red truck in the snow scene has a State of Texas inspection sticker on the windshield.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26798, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26840, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26844, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26846, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26848, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26850, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26851, 'The film was adapted from a play by the same authors, in which the female star of the film played all the roles, whether male or female.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26853, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26855, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26857, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26858, 'Official submission of Italy to the best foreign language film category of the 87th Academy Awards 2015.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26859, 'French visa# 136098.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26861, 'Movie
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26862, 'Carlo Mazzacurati''s last movie. It was released posthumously on 24 April 2014, 3 mouths later Mazzacurati''s death. Several actors of his previous movies enjoyed this one, making a cameo role.');
INSERT INTO imdb.text VALUES (26864, 'Movie
